inscript.</P></NOTE></HEAD> <COL N="0525"></COL> <P COM="0525"><NOTE N="I, 1." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0525" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0525"></COL> Initium evangelii Iesu Christi, filii Dei.</NOTE> <NOTE N="2." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0525" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0525"></COL> Ut scriptum est in Esaia profeta: ecce, ego mitto
angelum meum ante te, qui parat viam tuam ante te.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 2." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0525" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0525"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">faura þus</HI> ] sec. ante te,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.</NOTE>  Anastodeins aivanggeljons ïesuis xristaus sunaus guþs. sve gameliþ ïst ïn esaï ïn praufetau. sai.
 <NOTE N="3." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0525" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0525"></COL> Vox clamantis in deserto: parate viam domini,
rectas facite semitas Dei nostri!</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 3." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0525" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0525"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">guþs unsaris</HI> ] Dei nostri, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>auútouð.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  ik ïnsandja aggilu meinana faura þus. saei gamanveiþ vig þeinana faura þus. stibna vopjandins
 <NOTE N="4." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0525" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0525"></COL> Fuit Iohannes baptizans in deserto et nuntians baptismum poenitentiae
ad remissionem peccatorum;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 4." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0525" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0525"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">aflageinai</HI> ] sic cod. Arg. aperte; J. St. B. †
 <HI REND="ITALIC">aflateinai.</HI>  a Z. injuria probatum.</NOTE>  ïn auþidai. manveiþ vig fraujins. raihtos vaurkeiþ staigos guþs unsaris. vas ïohannes daupjands
 <NOTE N="5." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0525" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0525"></COL> et exierunt ad eum omnis Iudaea-terra et Ierusolymitani et baptizati
fuerunt omnes in Iordano aqua ab eo, confitentes peccata sua.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 5." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0525" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0525"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">usïddjedun</HI> ] exierunt, Ulf. aut c. gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxeporeuvonto</FOREIGN> 
legit, aut ex usu sermonis gothici vocem  <HI REND="ITALIC">land</HI> 
