 <HI REND="ITALIC">snaiys.—vullareis</HI> ] J. St. B. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">vuslareis.</HI></NOTE>  ïze. jah vastjos ïs vaurþun glitmunjandeins weitos sve snaivs. svaleikos sve vullareis ana airþai ni
 <NOTE N="4." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0553" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0553"></COL> Et visus fuit iis Helias cum Mose, et fuerunt loquentes cum Iesu.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IX, 4." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0554" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0554"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">varþ</HI> ] St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">qarþ.</HI></NOTE> <NOTE N="5." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0553" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0553"></COL> Et respondens
Petrus dixit ad Iesum: rabbi, bonum est nobis hic esse, et facimus tabernacula tria, tibi unum
 <COL N="0555"></COL> et Mosi unum et unum Heliae.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IX, 5." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0555" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0555"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ainana helijin</HI> ] ¶ gr. omn.</NOTE>  mag gaweitjan. jah ataugiþs varþ ïm helias miþ mose. jah vesun rodjandans miþ ïesua. jah andhafjands
