ïn þizai alh. ïþ þai auhmistans gudjans jah bokarjos sokidedun ïna usqistjan jah þai frumistans
 <NOTE N="48." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Et non invenerunt, quid facerent; turba enim prorsus suspensa-fuit ad audiendum eum.</NOTE> ; <NOTE N="XIX, 48." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">bigetun</HI> ] Ulf. c. codd.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tov.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">managei</HI> ]
J. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">managai.—alakjo hahaida</HI> ] J. St. B. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">allai gahahaida;</HI> 
caeterum de  <HI REND="ITALIC">alakjo</HI>  vid. ad vs. 37.— <HI REND="ITALIC">du hausjan</HI> ]
vid. ad XVIII, 35.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ïmma</HI> ] gr. omn. ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">du.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 1." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Et factumest
in quodam dierum illorum in docente eo hanc turbam in templo et evangelizante adsteterunt hi sacerdotes
et scribae cum his natu-maximis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 1." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">at laijandin</HI> ] J. St. Z. † jct.— <HI REND="ITALIC">sinistam</HI> ]
St †  <HI REND="ITALIC">sinistaim.</HI></NOTE>  manageins. jah ni bigetun wa gatavidedeina. managei auk alakjo habaida du hausjan ïmma. jah
varþ ïn sumamma dage jainaize at laisjandin ïmma þo managein ïn alh jah vailamerjandin atstoþun
 <NOTE N="2." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Et dixerunt ad eum dicentes: dic nobis, in qua potestatum hoc facis,
aut quis est, qui dedit tibi hanc potestatem?</NOTE>  þai gudjans jah bokarjos miþ þaim sinistam jah qeþun du ïmma qiþandans. qiþ unsis ïn wamma valdufnje
 <NOTE N="3." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Respondens autem dixit ad eos: interrogo vos etiam
ego unum verbum et dicite mihi:</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 3." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">andhafjands</HI> ] St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">andhafjadns.—fraihna</HI> ]
St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">fraina.</HI></NOTE>  þata taujis aiþþau was ïst saei gaf þus þata valdufni. andhafjands þan qaþ du ïm. fraihna
 <NOTE N="4." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> baptismus Iohannis exne coelo fuit an exne hominibus?</NOTE> <NOTE N="XX, 4." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">þau</HI> ] J. ÷  <HI REND="ITALIC">þauh.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="5." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Verum ii
cogitarunt cum se invicem dicentes: quod si dicimus, ex coelo, dicit, at cur non credidistis ei?</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 5." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">þahtedun</HI> ] St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">þahdedun.—aþþan.</HI> ] St.
†  <HI REND="ITALIC">aþþä</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">aþþa.</HI></NOTE>  ïzvis jah ïk ainis vaurdis jah qiþiþ mis. daupeins ïohannis uzuh himina vas þau uzuh mannam. ïþ
eis þahtedun miþ sis misso qiþandans. þatei jabai qiþam. us himina. qiþiþ. aþþan duwe ni galaubideduþ
 <NOTE N="6." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Verum si
dicimus, ex hominibus, omnis haec turba lapidibus conjicit nos, fideliter credunt enim omnes, Iohannem profetam
esse.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 6." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> [ <HI REND="ITALIC">allai</HI>  omnes,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.</NOTE>  ïmma. ïþ jabai qiþam. us mannam. alla so managei stainam afvairpiþ unsis. triggvaba galaubjand
 <NOTE N="7." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Et responderunt, quod non scirent unde.</NOTE> <NOTE N="XX, 7." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">vissedeina</HI> ] St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">vissedeinna.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="8." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Et lesus dixit iis, non ego vobis dico, in qua
potestatum hoc facio.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 8." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah</HI> ] pr., sic cod. Arg.; Hz. ÷  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïþ.—ïzvis
qiþa</HI> ] ¶ gr. omn.</NOTE>  auk allai ïohannen praufetu visan. jah andhofun ei ni vissedeina waþro. jah ïesus qaþ ïm. ni
 <NOTE N="9." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Coepit autem ad turbam dicere hanc parabolam: homo plantavit vineam et tradidit
eam colonis et abiit annos multos.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 9." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jera</HI> ] annos, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>crovnouû.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  ïk ïzvis qiþa ïn wamma valdufnje þata tauja. dugann þan du managein qiþan þo gajukon. manna ussatida
 <NOTE N="10." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0655" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0655"></COL> Et in tempore misit ad hos hortulanos servum, ut fructus hujus
 <COL N="0657"></COL> vineae darent ei; verum hi hortulani percutientes eum miserunt vacuum.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 10." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0656" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0656"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">gebeina</HI> ] St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">gebena.</HI></NOTE>  veinagard jah anafalh ïna vaurstvjam jah aflaiþ jera ganoha. jah ïn mela ïnsandida du þaim
aurtjam skalk. ei akranis þis veinagardis gebeina ïmma. ïþ þai aurtjans usbliggvandans ïna ïnsandidedun
 <COL N="0657"></COL> <NOTE N="11." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Et addidit mittere alium
servum, verum ii etiam illum percutientes et dehonorantes miserunt vacuum.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 11." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">anþarana</HI> ] J. St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">anþaran.</HI></NOTE>  lausana. jah anaaiauk sandjan anþarana skalk. ïþ eis jah jainana bliggvandans jah unsverandans
 <NOTE N="12." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Et addidit mittere tertium;
verum ii etiam hunc vulnerantes ejecerunt.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 12." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">gavondondans</HI> ] sic cod. Arg. et editt. pro
 <HI REND="ITALIC">gavundondans,</HI>  vid. ad IV, 13.</NOTE>  ïnsandidedun lausana. jah anaaiauk sandjan pridjan. ïþ eis jah þana gavondondans usvaurpun.
 <NOTE N="13." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Dixit autem hic dominus hujus vineae: quid faciam?
mitto filium meum hunc carum, forte hunc videntes aestimant.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 13." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">meinana</HI> ] J. St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">meinama.—liuban aufto</HI> ]
editt. et Hz. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">liubana ufto,</HI>  lectionem receptam Z. de
praestanti conjectura dedit; formam concretam, quam
vocant, articulus praepositus requirit, nec  <HI REND="ITALIC">ufto</HI>  nisi
cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïbai</HI>  conjunctum  <CITN>(si lectio M. XXVII, 64 proba
est)</CITN>  invenitur.</NOTE>  qaþ þan sa frauja þis veinagardis. wa taujau. sandja sunu meinana þana liuban. aufto þana
 <NOTE N="14." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Videntes autem eum hi hortulani cogitarunt
cum se invicem dicentes: hic est hic haeres; occidimus eum, ut nobis fiat haec haereditas.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 14." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">arbinumja</HI> ] Ulf. c. codd.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>deuðte.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  gasaiwandans aistand. gasaiwandans þan ïna þai aurtjans þahtedun miþ sis misso qiþandans. sa ïst
 <NOTE N="15." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Et
ejicientes eum foras ex hac vinea occiderunt. Quid nunc faciat iis dominus hujus vineae?</NOTE>  sa arbinumja. afslaham ïna. ei uns vairþai þata arbi. jah usvairpandans ïna ut us þamma veinagarda
 <NOTE N="16." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Venit et perdit
hortulanos hos et dat hanc vineam aliis. Audientes dixerunt autem: non sit.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 16." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">nis-sijai</HI> ] sic cod. Arg. Hz. Z.  <CITN>(vid. ad M.
V, 37)</CITN> ; J. St. B. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">ni sijai.</HI></NOTE>  usqemun. wa nu taujai ïm frauja þis veinagardis. qimiþ jah usqisteiþ aurtjam þaim jah gibiþ þana
 <NOTE N="17." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Verum is adspiciens ad
eos dixit: at quid est hoc scriptum, lapis, quem rejecerunt fabri, hic factus-est ad caput anguli?</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 17." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">stains</HI> ] lapis, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>livqon,</FOREIGN>  vid. ad Mc.
XII, 10.</NOTE>  veinagard anþaraim. gahausjandans qeþun þan. nis-sijai. ïþ ïs ïnsaiwands du ïm qaþ. aþþan wa ïst
 <NOTE N="18." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Quisque
qui cadit in hunc lapidem, conquassatur, verum in quem cadit, comminuit eum.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 18." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">gakrotuda</HI> ] vid. ad Mc. IX, 50.</NOTE>  þata gamelido. stains þammei uskusun timrjans. sah varþ du haubida vaihstins. wazuh saei driusiþ
 <NOTE N="19." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Et quaesiverunt hi scribae
et summi sacerdotes ponere in eum manus in hac hora et timuerunt hanc turbam; intellexerunt enim,
quod ad eos hanc parabolam dixit.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 19." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">bokarjos—gudjans</HI> ] ¶ gr.</NOTE>  ana þana stain. gakrotuda. ïþ ana þanei driusiþ disvinþeiþ ïna. jah sokidedun þai bokarjos jah auhumistans
gudjans uslagjan ana ïna handuns ïn þizai weilai jah ohtedun þo managein. froþun auk þatei
 <NOTE N="20." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Et discedentes miserunt insidiatores hos e dolo ostendentes se justos
esse, ut caperent eum ob-verba et traderent eum principatui et potestati praesidis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 20." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">afleiþandans</HI> ] discendentes, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parathrhvsanteû,</FOREIGN> 
Ulf. c. cod. D et verss.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpocwrhvsanteû</FOREIGN>  legit.— <HI REND="ITALIC">us
liutein</HI> ] J. St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">usanigein,</HI>  B. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">us anigein;</HI> 
veram lectionem jam Maresh. p. 462 et L. dederunt.— <HI REND="ITALIC">jah
atgebeina</HI> ] et traderent, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû toú (wåste)
 <COL N="0658"></COL> paradouðnai</FOREIGN> ; Ulf. c. verss. lat.</NOTE>  du ïm þo gajukon qaþ. jah afleiþandans ïnsandidedun ferjans þans us liutein taiknjandans sik garaihtans
 <NOTE N="21." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Et interrogarunt
eum dicentes: magister, scimus, quod recte loqueris et doces et non respicis faciem, sed in veritate viam
Dei doces:</NOTE>  visan. ei gafaifaheina ïs vaurde jah atgebeina ïna reikja jah valdufnja kindinis. jah frehun
ïna qiþandans. laisari. vitum þatei raihtaba rodeis jah laiseis jah ni andsaiwis andvairþi ak bi sunjai
 <NOTE N="22." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> debitumne est nobis Caesari tributum dare an nonne?</NOTE> <NOTE N="XX, 22." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">skuldu</HI> ] J. St. ÷  <HI REND="ITALIC">skuld.—kaisara gild</HI> ] B.
Hz. Z. ÷ jct., quod quamquam loco Mc. XII, 14 comprobatum,
h. l. textui graeco ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaivsari fovron</FOREIGN> ) non respondet.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="23." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Perspiciens autem eorum improbitatem
Iesus dixit ad eos: quid me tentatis?</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 23." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">unselein</HI> ] Ulf. c. codd. pro vulg.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>panourgivan</FOREIGN> 
legisse videtur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ponhrivan,</FOREIGN>  vid. Mc. VII, 22; Cor.
I, V, 8; Eph. VI, 12; cf. Eph. IV, 31.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ïesus</HI> ]  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.</NOTE>  vig guþs laiseis. skuldu ïst unsis kaisara gild giban þau niu. bisaiwands þan ïze unselein ïesus qaþ
 <NOTE N="24." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Ostendite mihi nummum, cujus habet effigiem et inscriptionem?
Respondentes autem dixerunt: Caesaris.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 24." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">mis</HI> ] J. St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">mik.</HI></NOTE>  du ïm. wa mik fraisiþ. ataugeiþ mis skatt. wis habaiþ manleikan jah ufarmeli. andhafjandans þan
 <NOTE N="25." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Verum is dixit ad eos: igitur reddite haec Caesaris
Caesari et haec Dei Deo.</NOTE> <NOTE N="XX, 25." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">us nu gibiþ</HI> ] vid. ad Mc. XIV, 44.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="26." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Et non potuerunt capere eum ob-verba in praesentia turbae et mirantes ob-responsa
ejus tacuerunt.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 26." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">andavaurde</HI> ] responsa, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpokrivsei</FOREIGN> ;
caeterum J. St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">andvaurde.</HI></NOTE>  qeþun. kaisaris. ïþ ïs qaþuh du ïm. us nu gibiþ þo kaisaris kaisara jah þo guþs guþa. jah ni mahtedun
 <NOTE N="27." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Accedentes autem quidam Sadducaeorum, qui dicunt, resurrectionem non esse,
interrogaverunt eum</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 27." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">qiþand</HI> ] gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajntilevgonteû,</FOREIGN>  Ulf. c. codd.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>levgonteû</FOREIGN> 
legit.</NOTE>  gafahan ïs vaurde ïn andvairþja manageins jah sildaleikjandans andavaurde ïs gaþahaidedun.
 <NOTE N="28." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> dicentes: magister, Moses scripsit nobis, si cujus frater moriatur habens uxorem
et hic sine-prole moriatur, ut ducat frater ejus hanc uxorem et suscitet semen fratri suo;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 28." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïs</HI> ] J. St. B.  <SUP>o</SUP>  †.</NOTE>  duatgaggandans þan sumai saddukaie. þaiei qiþand usstass ni visan. frehun ïna qiþandans. laisari.
moses gamelida uns. jabai wis broþar gadauþnai aigands qen jah sa unbarnahs gadauþnai. ei nimai
 <NOTE N="29." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> septem igitur
fratres fuerunt et hic primus ducens uxorem mortuus-est sine-prole.</NOTE>  broþar ïs þo qen jah urraisjai fraiv broþr seinamma. sibun nu broþrjus vesun jah sa frumista
 <NOTE N="30." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Et duxit alter hanc uxorem et hic
obiit sine-prole.</NOTE> <NOTE N="31." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Et tertius duxit hanc similiter; similiter autem etiam hi septem et non reliquerunt
liberos et obierunt.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 31." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">samaleiko</HI> ] pr. similiter,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.— <HI REND="ITALIC">jah</HI> ] tert.
et  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.</NOTE>  nimands qen gadauþnoda unbarnahs. jah nam anþar þo qen jah sa gasvalt unbarnahs. jah þridja nam
 <NOTE N="32." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> Ultima omnium mortua-est etiam haec uxor.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 32." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">spedista</HI> ] ultima, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uåsteron</FOREIGN> ; caeterum
Ulf. c. codd.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  þo samaleiko. samaleiko þan jah þai sibun jah ni biliþun barne jah gasvultun. spedista allaize gadauþnoda
 <NOTE N="33." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0657" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0657"></COL> In hac resurrectione igitur cujus
 <COL N="0659"></COL> horum fituxor? hi enim septem habuerunt hanc ad uxorem.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 33." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0658" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0658"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">nu</HI> ] gr. omn. ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">usstassai.—vaïrþiþ</HI> ] fit
Sch. temere contendit, Gothum legisse  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæstai.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  jah so qens. ïn þizai usstassai nu warjis þize vairþiþ qens. þai auk sibun aihtedun þo du
 <COL N="0659"></COL> <NOTE N="34." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0659" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0659"></COL> Et respondens dixit ad eos Iesus, hi filii hujus
aevi nubunt et nubuntur:</NOTE> <NOTE N="35." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0659" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0659"></COL> verum qui digni sunt illud aevum nancisci et resurrectionem e mortuis, non
nubunt, non nubuntur,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XX, 35." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0659" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0659"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">þaiei</HI> ] J. St. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">þatei.—usstassais</HI> ] St. †
