 <NOTE N="13." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0709" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0709"></COL> Tunc Pilatus audiens haec——</NOTE>   <NOTE N="XIX, 13." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0710" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0710"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">þize</HI> ] haec (verba), gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touðton (toún lovgon</FOREIGN> ).</NOTE>  ïzei þiudan sik silban taujiþ. andstandiþ kaisara. þanuh peilatus hausjands þize——</P></DIV2></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0709" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0709">EPISTOLAE.</HEAD> <DIV2 COM="0709" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0709">DU RUMONIM.</HEAD> <P COM="0709"><NOTE N="VI, 23." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0709" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0709"></COL> —haec enim stipendia peccati mors, verum gratia Dei vita aeterna in Christo Iesu, domino nostro.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VI, 23-XI,33" TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0709" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0709"></COL> leguntur in cod. Ambros. A.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VI, 23." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0709" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0709"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">auk launa</HI> ] hanc nostram conjecturam Cast.,
qui ipse  <HI REND="ITALIC">mikiluna</HI>  ediderat, auctoritate codicis A denuo
inspecti probari confitetur. Articuli autem insolitus
usus nunc non offendit, vid. XIII, 3  <HI REND="ITALIC">þai auk
reiks.</HI>  X, 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">sa raihtis vilja.</HI></NOTE> —þo auk launa fravaurhtais dauþus. ïþ ansts guþs libains aiveino ïn xristau ïesu fraujin unsa
 <NOTE N="VII, 1." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0709" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0709"></COL> Aut nonne scitis, fratres, scientibus enim legem loquor, quod lex regit hominem tam longum tempus
quam vivit?</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 1." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0709" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0709"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">mann sva</HI> ] cod. A et Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">manns:</HI>  primum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">mann</HI>  dativum constructio  <HI REND="ITALIC">fraujinon</HI>  verbi requirit;
deinde  <HI REND="ITALIC">sva,</HI>  cujus nullum vestigium in cod.
A cognosci Cast. dicit, ex parte tantum a librario
omissum est, nam  <HI REND="ITALIC">s</HI>  legitur, cf. vs. 25, ubi pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïk</HI> 
librarius omisso  <HI REND="ITALIC">k</HI>  solummodo  <HI REND="ITALIC">ï</HI>  scripsit; aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">va</HI>  litterae
fortasse in margine scriptae litura interierunt.</NOTE>  ramma. þau niu vituþ. broþrjus. kunnandam auk vitoþ rodja. þatei vitoþ fraujinoþ mann sva lagga
 <NOTE N="2." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0709" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0709"></COL> Et enim sub viro mulier in vivente marito ligata est lege, at si moritur maritus, liberatur
ab hac lege mariti.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 2." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0709" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0709"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah auk</HI> ] etenim, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gavr,</FOREIGN>  sic Cor. I,
XV, 16  <HI REND="ITALIC">jah jabai auk</HI>  =  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eij gavr.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">uf va ra</HI> ] aegre desideramus
 <COL N="0710"></COL> articulum  <HI REND="ITALIC">so,</HI>  quem hac verborum structura
