Goth. c. codd.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpistolhv.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">dustodeiþ</HI> ]
incipit,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn. Pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">dustodeiþ</HI>  in inscriptionibus
evangeliorum Marci et Lucae et epistolae
ad Ephesios  <HI REND="ITALIC">anastodeiþ</HI>  legitur.</P></NOTE></HEAD> <COL N="0749"></COL> <P COM="0749"><NOTE N="I, 1." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0749" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0749"></COL> Pavlus apostolus Iesu Christi per voluntatem Dei et Timotheus frater ecclesiae Dei huic existenti
in Corintho cum omnibus his sanctis his existentibus in omni Acaeja;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 1." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0750" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0750"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">allaim</HI> ] gr. omn. post  <HI REND="ITALIC">veiham.—akaijai</HI> ] sic
cod. B pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">akajai,</HI>  vid. IX, 2; sic etiam I, XVI, 15
 <HI REND="ITALIC">akaije</HI>  legitur pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">akaje,</HI>  vid. infra XI, 10.</NOTE>  Pavlus apaustaulus ïesuis xristaus þairh viljan guþs jah teimauþaius broþar aikklesjon guþs þizai
 <NOTE N="2." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0749" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0749"></COL> gratia vobis et pax a Deo, patre
 <COL N="0751"></COL> nostro et domino Iesu Christo;</NOTE>  visandein ïn kaurinþon miþ allaim þaim veiham þaim visandam ïn allai akaijai. ansts ïzvis jah gavairþi
 <COL N="0751"></COL> <NOTE N="3." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> venerandus Deus et pater domini nostri Iesu Christi, pater misericordiarum
et Deus omnium consolationum,</NOTE>  fram guþa attin unsaramma jah fraujin ïesu xristau. þiuþiþs guþ jah atta fraujins unsaris ïesuis
 <NOTE N="4." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> qui consolatus-est nos in omni sollicitudine nostra, ut possimus
nos consolari hos in omnibus sollicitudinibus per hanc consolationem qua requieti sumus ipsi a Deo.</NOTE>  xristaus atta bleiþeino jah guþ allaizo gaþlaihte. saei gaþrafstida uns ana allai aglon unsarai ei
mageima veis gaþrafstjan þans ïn allaim aglom þairh þo gaþlaiht. þizaiei gaþrafstidai sijum silbans
 <NOTE N="5." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> Nam sicut abundantia est passionum Christi in nobis, sic etiam per Christum super multum est etiam
consolatio nostra.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 5." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah</HI> ] pr. etiam,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.</NOTE>  fram guþa. unte svasve ufarassus ïst þulaine xristaus ïn uns sva jah þairh xristu ufar filu ïst jah gaþrafsteins
 <NOTE N="6." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> At sive tribulamur propter vestram consolationem et salutem hanc efficacem in tolerantiam
harum earumdem passionum, quas etiam nos patimur et spes nostra stabilita pro vobis; sive requiescimus
propter vestram consolationem et salutem,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 6." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jaþþe gaþrafstjanda.—naseinais</HI> ] gr. ante
 <HI REND="ITALIC">þizos vaurstveigons</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">jah naseinais.</HI></NOTE>  unsara. aþþan jaþþe þreihanda ïn ïzvaraizos gaþlaihtais jah naseinais þizos vaurstveigons
ïn stivitja þizo samono þulaine þozei jah veis vinnam jah vens unsara gatulgida faur ïzvis. jaþþe
 <NOTE N="7." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> scientes, quod sicut socii passionum estis, etiam consolationis
fitis;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 7." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">sijuþ</HI> ] gr. omn. ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">þulaine;</HI>  caeterum Goth.
 <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouåtw.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">vairþiþ</HI> ] fitis,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.</NOTE>  gaþrafstjanda ïn ïzvaraizos gaþlaihtais jah naseinais. vitandans þatei svasve gadailans pulaine sijuþ
 <NOTE N="8." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> nam non volumus vos inscios, fratres, de sollicitudine nostra hac facta nobis in Asia,
nam supramodum gravati fuimus super facultatem, adeo-ut taederet nos etiam vivere;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 8." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">unveisans</HI> ] inscios, scil.  <HI REND="ITALIC">visan.—svasve</HI> ] inde
usque IV, 10  <HI REND="ITALIC">unsaramma</HI>  etiam in cod. A leguntur.— <HI REND="ITALIC">svasve.—liban</HI> ]
cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">svasve afsvaggvidai veseima
jal-liban</HI>  (adeo-ut haesitantes essemus etiam vivere)
«indicatur tamen et altera lectio in margine sic . . .
 <HI REND="ITALIC">maide . . . </HI>  iterumque inferius in eodem margine  <HI REND="ITALIC">skamaidedeima.</HI> »  <ED>CAST.</ED></NOTE>  jah gaþlaihtais vairþiþ. unte ni vileima ïzvis unveisans. broþrjus. bi aglon unsara þo vaurþanon
 <NOTE N="9." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> sed ipsi in nobis
ipsis responsionem mortis habuimus, ut non simus fidentes in nos ipsos, sed in Deum hunc suscitantem
mortuos,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 9." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">sijaima trauandans</HI> ] ¶ gr. omn.</NOTE>  uns ïn asiai. unte ufarassau kauridai vesum ufar maht svasve skamaidedeima uns jah liban. akei
silbans ïn uns silbam andahaft dauþaus habaidedum. ei nisijaima trauandans du uns silbam ak du
 <NOTE N="10." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> qui a talibus mortibus nos liberavit et liberat, in quo speravimus, quod liberat.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 10." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">svaleikaim dauþum</HI> ] talibus mortibus, gr.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thlikouvtou qanavtou.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">uns galausida</HI> ] ¶ gr. omn.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ei</HI> ]
Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú eæti.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  guþa þamma urraisjandin dauþans. ïzei us svaleikaim dauþum uns galausida jah galauseiþ. du þammei
 <NOTE N="11." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> In adjuvantibus
etiam vobis pro nobis precatione, ut in multa praesentia haec in nobis donatio per multos gratecommemoretur
pro nobis;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 11." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïn managamma andvairþja</HI> ] in multa praesentia,
gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejk pollwðn proswvpwn.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  venidedum ei galauseiþ. at hilpandam jah ïzvis bi uns bidai ei ïn managamma andvairþja so ïn
 <NOTE N="12." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> nam gloria nostra hoc est testimonium conscientiae nostrae, quod in simplicitate
et sinceritate Dei, non in sapientia carnali, sed in gratia Dei versati-sumus in hoc mundo, verum
supramodum apud vos.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 12." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">hlutrein</HI> ] sic codd. h. I. et II, 17  <HI REND="ITALIC">hlutriþai.</HI> 
VII, 11  <HI REND="ITALIC">hlutrans;</HI>  Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">hautrein, hautriþai, hautrans.—usmetum</HI> ]
cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">usmeitum.</HI></NOTE>  uns giba þairh managans aviliudodau faur uns. unte woftuli unsara so ïst veitvodei miþvisseins
unsaraizos. þatei ïn ainfalþein jah hlutrein guþs ni ïn handugein leikeinai ak ïn anstai guþs usmetum
 <NOTE N="13." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> Nam non alia scribimus vobis, sed quae legitis aut etiam cognoscitis; at spero,
quod usque finem cognoscitis,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 13." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">alja</HI> ] sec. ||  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajll1 hæ,</FOREIGN>  cf. Mc. IX, 8 ubi etiam
pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajllav</FOREIGN>  varia lectio  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajll1 hæ</FOREIGN>  est.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ei</HI> ] Goth. c. codd.
 <COL N="0752"></COL> <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  ïn þamma fairwau ïþ ufarassau at ïzvis. unte ni alja meljam ïzvis alja þoei anakunnaiþ aiþþau
 <NOTE N="14." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> sicut cognovistis nos de quodam, nam gloria vestra sumus, sicut etiam vos
nostra in die domini Iesu Christi.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 14." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0752" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0752"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">svasve</HI> ] pro Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">xristaus</HI> ]  <SUP>o</SUP>  cod. A
c. gr.</NOTE>  jah ufkunnaiþ. aþþan venja ei und andi ufkunnaiþ. svasve gakunnaideduþ uns bi sumata. unte
 <NOTE N="15." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> Et hac confidentia volui prius venire ad vos, ut alteram gratiam
haberetis,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 15." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0752" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0752"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">faurþis.—ïzvis</HI> ] ¶ gr.</NOTE>  woftuli ïzvara sijum svasve jah jus unsara ïn daga fraujins ïesuis xristaus. jah þizai trauainai vilda
 <NOTE N="16." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> et per vos ire in Macidoniam et rursus a Macidonia venire ad vos et a vobis deducere me in
Iudaeam.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 16." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0752" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0752"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah þairh</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">jaþ-þairh.—makidonja</HI> ]
cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">makaidonja,</HI>  sic idem II, 13 paulo infra et VII,
5  <HI REND="ITALIC">makaidonjai;</HI>  quam varietatem lectionis non inde
natam esse existimamus, uti Castil., quod Graecis et
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Makhdoniva</FOREIGN>  et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Makedoniva</FOREIGN>  scribere mos fuisset, quarum
formarum alteram cod. B. per  <HI REND="ITALIC">makidonja</HI>  (quia Ulfilae
aetate  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>h</FOREIGN>  uti  <HI REND="ITALIC">i</HI>  pronuntiatum esset), alteram cod. A
per  <HI REND="ITALIC">makaidonja</HI>  reddidisset; neutiquam enim Graeci
illis formis promiscue utebantur, sed  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Makhdoniva</FOREIGN>  metri
rationibus expostulatum apud solos poetas invenitur;
potius  <HI REND="ITALIC">makidonja</HI>  formam insolentiorem esse
judicamus, nec quidquam in promptu est cum quo
comparari possit, praeter  <HI REND="ITALIC">aggiljus</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">aggeljus</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæggeloi</FOREIGN> ).</NOTE>  faurþis qiman at ïzvis ei anþara anst habaidedeip. jah þairh ïzvis galeiþan ïn makidonja jah aftra af
 <NOTE N="17." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> Hoc vero igitur cogitans, num fortasse levitate usus-sum aut quod cogito, secundum carnem
putem, ut non sit apud me hoc sane, sane! et hoc minime, minime!</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 17." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0752" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0752"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ni</HI> ] non,  <SUP>o</SUP>  cod. A c. gr. omn.</NOTE>  makidonjai qiman at ïzvis jah fram ïzvis gasandjan mik in ïudaia. þatuþþan nu mitonds ïbai aufto
 <NOTE N="18." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> At fidelis Deus, quod hoc verbum
nostrum, hoc ad vos, non-est sane et minime;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 18." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0752" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0752"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">nist.</HI> ] non est, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujk ejgevneto.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">jah ne</HI> ] cod.
A  <HI REND="ITALIC">jan-ne.</HI></NOTE>  leihtis bruhta. aiþþau þatei mito. bi leika þagkjau ei ni sijai at mis þata ja ja jah þata ne ne. aþþan
 <NOTE N="19." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0751" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0751"></COL> nam Dei filius, Iesus Christus, qui in vobis per nos praedicatur,
 <COL N="0753"></COL> per me et Silbanum et Timotheum, non factus-est sane et minime, sed sane in eo factum-est.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 19." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0752" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0752"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">vailamerjada</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">merjada.—teimauþaiu</HI> ]
sic recte cod. B; cod. A †  <HI REND="ITALIC">teimaiþaiu.—nih</HI> ] cod.
A  <HI REND="ITALIC">ni.—jah ne</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">jan-ne.</HI></NOTE>  triggvs guþ ei þata vaurd unsar þata du ïzvis nist ja jah ne. unte guþs sunus ïesus xristus. saei ïn
ïzvis þairh uns vailamerjada þairh mik jah silbanu jah teimauþaiu. nih varþ ja jah ne ak ja ïn ïmma
 <COL N="0753"></COL> <NOTE N="20." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> Quam multae promissiones Dei in eo hoc sane, ideo etiam per eum amen Deo ad gloriam per nos.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 20." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">waiva</HI> ] Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gavr.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">duþþe—ïna</HI> ] ideo—eum,
gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejn aujtwðé</FOREIGN> ; caeterum pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">jah þairh</HI>  cod.
A  <HI REND="ITALIC">jaþ-þairh.</HI></NOTE>  varþ. waiva managa gahaita guþs ïn ïmma þata ja. duþþe jah þairh ïna amen guþa du vulþau þairh
 <NOTE N="21." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> At hic
confirmans nos cum vobis in Christo et ungens nos Deus;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 21." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">unsis</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">uns.—salbonds</HI> ] cod. A †  <HI REND="ITALIC">salbonsd.</HI></NOTE> <NOTE N="22." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> et signans nos et dans pignus spiritum in
corda nostra.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 22." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ahman</HI> ] spiritum, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pneuvmatoû</FOREIGN>  pendens
a  <HI REND="ITALIC">vadi,</HI>  c. Goth. patres esse latinos, qui eamdem
lectionem sequantur, Mill. testatur.</NOTE>  uns. aþþan sa gaþvastjands unsis miþ ïzvis ïn xristau jah salbonds uns guþ. jah sigljands uns jah
 <NOTE N="23." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> At ego testem Deum invoco contra meam animam, quod parcens vobis amplius non veni
in Corinthum,</NOTE>  gibands vadi ahman ïn hairtona unsara. aþþan ïk veitvod guþ anahaita ana meinai saivalai ei freidjands
 <NOTE N="24." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> non quod imperamus vestrae fidei, sed adjutores sumus gratiae vestrae, nam fide stetistis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="I, 24." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">fraujinoma</HI> ] sic recte cod. A; cod. B †  <HI REND="ITALIC">fraujoma.—anstai</HI> ]
gratiae,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>caraðû,</FOREIGN>  Goth. c. codd. 37 et
71  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>cavritoû,</FOREIGN>  legentibus consentit.</NOTE>  ïzvara þanaseiþs ni qam ïn kaurinþon. ni þatei fraujinoma ïzvarai galaubeinai ak gavaurstvans
 <NOTE N="II, 1." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> At statui hoc ipsum apud me, ut iterum in moerore non veniam ad vos;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 1." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">þata—mis</HI> ] hoc ipsum apud me, gr. omn.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejmautwðé touðto,</FOREIGN>  in quo non solum transpositio verborum,
verum etiam Gothum interpretari, quasi  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toú aujtov</FOREIGN> 
(I.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touðto aujtoú) ejmoiv</FOREIGN>  legisset, notandum est.— <HI REND="ITALIC">qimau</HI> ]
gr. post  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvis.</HI></NOTE>  sijum anstais ïzvaraizos. unte galaubeinai gastoþuþ. aþþan gastauïda þata silbo at mis ei aftra
 <NOTE N="2." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> nam si ego contristo vos,
et quis est qui delectet me, nisi hic contristatus a me?</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 2." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">nibai</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">niba.</HI></NOTE>  ïn saurgai ni qimau at ïzvis. unte jabai ïk gaurja ïzvis jah was ïst saei gailjai mik nibai sa gaurida
 <NOTE N="3." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> Et hoc ipsum scripsi vobis, ut veniens moerorem
non habeam de quibus debui gaudere, confidens in omnibus vobis, quod meum gaudium omnium vestri est.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 3." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah þata</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">jaþ-þata.—þata silbo</HI> ] gr.
post  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvis.—faheds</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">faheþs.</HI></NOTE>  us mis. jah þata silbo gamelida ïzvis ei qimands saurga ni habau. fram þaimei skulda faginon gatrauands
 <NOTE N="4." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> At e multa afflictione et angore cordis scripsi vobis per multas lacrymas, non ut moereatis, sed ut amorem
cognoscatis quem habeo abundanter ad vos.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 4." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ak ei</HI> ] Cast. † jct., caeterum  <HI REND="ITALIC">ei</HI>  gr. omn. post
 <HI REND="ITALIC">friaþva.—friaþva</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">frijaþva.</HI></NOTE>  ïn allaim ïzvis þatei meina faheds allaize ïzvara ïst. aþþan us managai aglon jah aggviþai
hairtins gamelida ïzvis þairh managa tagra ni þeei saurgaiþ ak ei friaþva kunneiþ. þoei haba ufarassau
 <NOTE N="5." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> At si quis contristavit, non me contristavit, sed ex parte, ut
non onerem omnes vos.</NOTE>  du ïzvis. aþþan jabai was gaurida. ni mik gaurida ak bi sumata ei ni anakaurjau allans ïzvis.
 <NOTE N="6." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> Sufficiens huic tali vituperium hoc a pluribus,</NOTE> <NOTE N="7." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> Adeo ut hoc contrarium vos
magis donetis et consolemini, ne forte pluri moerore absumatur hic talis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 7." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0753" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0753"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvis mais</HI> ] ¶ gr.— <HI REND="ITALIC">jah gaþlaihan</HI> ] cod. A
