gaþlaihtai þizaiei gaþrafstiþs vas ana ïzvis gateihands uns ïzvara gairnein ïzvarana gaunoþa ïzvar
 <NOTE N="8." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> Nam si contristavi vos in his litteris, non poenitet me, et si poenituit, video enim quod haec
epistola illa si ad paucum tempus contristavit vos,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 8." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jabai</HI> ] Goth. c. cod. c. ap. Mi.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">þaim</HI> ]
 <SUP>o</SUP>  cod. A.— <HI REND="ITALIC">jah jabai</HI> ] gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eij kaiv,</FOREIGN>  formula hoc
verborum ordine invenitur etiam XII, 11, cum L.
XVIII, 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">jabai jah</HI>  legatur.— <HI REND="ITALIC">gasaiwa auk</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">unte
gasaiwa</HI>  (nam video).— <HI REND="ITALIC">dulleitilai</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">du leitilai;</HI> 
lectio recepta, quod jam Cast. adnotavit, pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">duh
leitilai</HI>   <CITN>(vid. ad Cor. I, VII, 16)</CITN> , cui inest  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv</FOREIGN>  particula
( <HI REND="ITALIC">-uh</HI> ); nam etsi ad J. XVIII, 26  <HI REND="ITALIC">uh</HI>  encliticum pro
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">etiam</HI>  significante particula poni posse negavimus,
tamen eos locos excipimus quibus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv</FOREIGN>  cum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eij</FOREIGN>  conjungitur;
his enim Goth.  <HI REND="ITALIC">jah</HI>  aut plane omittit, aut
 <COL N="0764"></COL> ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">jabai</HI>  ponit (vid. supra), unde his locis Goth. in illo  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv</FOREIGN>  gravem quemdam sensum non posuisse apparet;
caeterum  <HI REND="ITALIC">leitilai</HI>  (paucum)  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn. neque
Joan. V, 35; Phil. 15 additur; dicitur autem Skeir.
p. 47, 3  <HI REND="ITALIC">du leitilamma mela.</HI></NOTE>  aljan faur mik svaei mis mais faginon varþ. unte jabai gaurida ïzvis ïn þaim bokom. ni ïdreigo mik
 <NOTE N="9." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> nunc gaudeo, non quia contristati fuistis, sed quod
contristati fuistis ad poenitentiam. Moeruistis enim secundum Deum, ut in quoquam non castigemini a nobis,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 9." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0764" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0764"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">saurgaideduþ</HI> ] sic recte cod. A; cod. B †
 <HI REND="ITALIC">saurgideduþ.—ïn</HI> ]  <SUP>o</SUP>  cod. A.</NOTE>  jah jabai ïdreigoda. gasaiwa auk þatei so aipistaule jaina jabai dul-leitilai weilai gaurida ïzvis. nu
fagino. ni unte gauridai vesuþ ak unte gauridai vesuþ du ïdreigai. saurgaideduþ auk bi guþ ei ïn
 <NOTE N="10." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> nam hic secundum Deum moeror poenitentiam ad salutem firmam efficit, verum hujus mundi moeror
mortem parat.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 10." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0764" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0764"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">so</HI> ]  <SUP>o</SUP>  cod. A.— <HI REND="ITALIC">gatulgidai</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">gatulgida</HI> 
ad  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïdreiga</HI>  relatum, cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">gatulgidai</HI>  ad  <HI REND="ITALIC">ganistai</HI>  referendum
sit.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ustiuhada</HI> ] vid. ad J. XIII, 35.— <HI REND="ITALIC">du
teitau</HI>  ad Titum. gr,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiú Tivtou</FOREIGN> ; Goth. c. codd.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>provû
Tivton.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  vaihtai ni gasleiþjaindau us unsis. unte so bi guþ saurga ïdreiga du ganistai gatulgidai ustiuhada
 <NOTE N="11." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> Vide enim ipsum hoc secundum Deum moerere vos quantam perfecit vobis sollicitudinem,
sed defensionem, sed indignationem, sed timorem, sed desiderium, sed studium, sed vindictam; in
omni praestitistis vos puros esse hoc opere.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 11." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0764" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0764"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">saiw</HI> ] cod. A †  <HI REND="ITALIC">saiwa</HI>  (video).— <HI REND="ITALIC">hlutrans</HI> ]
sic codd.; Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">hautrans,</HI>  vid. ad I, 12.— <HI REND="ITALIC">visan</HI> ]
Goth. c. codd.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  ïþ þis fairwaus saurga dauþu gasmiþoþ. saiw auk silbo þata bi guþ saurgan ïzvis welauda gatavida
ïzvis usdaudein akei sunjon akei unverein akei agis akei gairnein akei aljan akei fraveit. ïn allamma
 <NOTE N="12." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> At si scripsi non propter hunc injuria-afficientem, non
propter hunc injuria-affectum, sed ad ostendendum sollicitudinem nostram, quam pro vobis habemus erga
vos in facie Dei.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 12." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0764" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0764"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jabai</HI> ] Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">melida</HI> ] Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJmiðn.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  ustaiknideduþ ïzvis hlutrans visan þamma toja. aþþan jabai melida ni ïn þis anamahtjandins ni ïn
þis anamahtidins ak du gabairhtjan usdaudein unsara. þoei faur ïzvis habam viþra ïzvis ïn and
 <NOTE N="13." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> Propter hoc moniti sumus, at in consolatione nostra multo magis gavisi-sumus de
gaudio Titi, nam refectus fuit spiritus ejus ab omnibus vobis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 13." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0764" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0764"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïnuh þis</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïnuþ-þis.—sium</HI> ] cod.
A  <HI REND="ITALIC">sijum.—aþþan</HI> ] at,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.; Goth. conspirat cum iis
codd. qui  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev</FOREIGN>  h. l. ponunt et infra post  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>perissovteroû</FOREIGN> 
( <HI REND="ITALIC">filaus</HI> ) omittunt.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ana</HI> ] pr.  <SUP>o</SUP>  cod. A.— <HI REND="ITALIC">unsarai</HI> ]
nostra, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJmwðn.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  vairþja guþs. ïnuh þis gaþrafstidai sium aþþan ana gaþrafsteinai unsarai filaus mais faginodedun
 <NOTE N="14." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> Nam si quid ei de vobis gloriatus sum, non
pudore affectus fui, sed sicut omne vobis in veritate locuti-sumus, sic etiam gloriatio nostra haec ad Titum
veritas fuit,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 14." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0764" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0764"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvis</HI> ] gr. omn. post  <HI REND="ITALIC">rodidedum.</HI></NOTE>  ana fahedai teitaus. unte anaweilaiþs varþ ahma ïs fram allaim ïzvis. unte jabai wa ïmma fram
ïzvis waiwop. ni gaaiviskoþs varþ ak svasve allata ïzvis ïn sunjai rodidedum sva jah woftuli unsara
 <NOTE N="15." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> et viscera ejus abundanter ad vos sunt reminiscentis hoc omnium vestrum obsequium, ut
cum timore et tremore suscepistis eum.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 15." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0764" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0764"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah brusts</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">jab-brusts.—ïna</HI> ] sic
recte cod. A; cod. B †  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïne.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="16." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> Gaudeo igitur, nam in omni confido in vos.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VII, 16." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0764" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0764"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">nu</HI> ] igitur,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.</NOTE>  so du teitau sunja varþ. jah brusts is ufarassau du ïzvis sind gamunandins þo allaize ïzvara ufhausein
 <NOTE N="VIII, 1." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0763" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0763"></COL> At notifico
 <COL N="0765"></COL> vobis, fratres, gratiam Dei hanc datam in ecclesia Macidoniae.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 1." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0764" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0764"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">kannja</HI> ] notifico, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gnwrivzomen.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">aikklesjon</HI> ]
sic cod. B; cod. A omnino melius cum gr. omn.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">aikklesjom</HI>  (ecclesiis).</NOTE>  sve miþ agisa jah reiron andnemuþ ïna. fagino nu unte ïn allamma gatraua ïn ïzvis. aþþan kannja
 <COL N="0765"></COL> <NOTE N="2." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> quod in multo experimento tristitiae multitudo
gaudii eorum et haec profunda paupertas eorum abundavit ad divitias simplicitatis eorum;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 2." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah þata</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">jaþ-þata.</HI></NOTE>  ïzvis. broþrjus. ants guþs þo gibanon ïn aikklesjon makidonais. þatei ïn managamma kustau aglons
 <NOTE N="3." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> nam secundum
virtutem testor et supra virtutem voluntarii fuerunt,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 3." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">silbaviljos</HI> ] quod adverbiumme esset  <CITN>(uti
 <HI REND="ITALIC">aljaleikos</HI>  Philipp. III, 15)</CITN> , an adjectivum, cum Cast.
dubitasset, Grim. W. J. p. 202 et Gram. III, 596
pluralem substantivi esse recte monuit, rectius autem
pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">silbavilis</HI>  formam  <HI REND="ITALIC">silbavileis</HI>  posuisset, vid.
Gram. l, 599 sq.— <HI REND="ITALIC">vesun</HI> ] fuerunt,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.</NOTE>  managduþs fahedais ïze jah þata diupo unledi ïze usmanagnoda du gabein ainfalþeins ïze. unte bi mahtai
 <NOTE N="4." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> cum multa exhortatione precantes nos accipere gratiam
suam et communicationem ministerii in hos sanctos.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 4." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">usbloteinai</HI> ] cod. B †  <HI REND="ITALIC">usbloþeinai.—niman</HI> ]
accipere,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr., qui habent cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">uns</HI>  post  <HI REND="ITALIC">veihans</HI> 
ponunt; Ulf. c. Ambrst.— <HI REND="ITALIC">seina</HI> ] suam,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.
omn. cf. ad l, VII, 16.</NOTE>  veitvodja jah ufar maht silbaviljos vesun. miþ managai usbloteinai bidjandans uns niman
 <NOTE N="5." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> Et non sicut speravimus, sed se ipsos dederunt
primum Domino, deinde autem nobis per voluntatem Dei,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 5." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah ni</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">jan-ni.—þaþroh þan</HI> ] cod.
A  <HI REND="ITALIC">þaþroþ-þan,</HI>  caeterum gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv</FOREIGN> ; Goth. c.
verss. lat., cf. tamen L. IV, 9, ubi  <HI REND="ITALIC">þaþroh</HI>  =
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  anst seina jah gamainein andbahtjis ïn þans veihans. jah ni svasve venidedum ak sik silbans
 <NOTE N="6." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> adeo-ut precaremur Titum, ut sicut antea
incepit, sic perficiat in vos etiam hanc gratiam.</NOTE>  atgebun frumist fraujin. þaþroh þan uns þairh viljan guþs. svaei bedeima teitaun ei svasve
 <NOTE N="7." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> Sed uti quidem in omni abundatis, fide et verbo et
cognitione et in omni sollicitudine et in hac e vobis in nos caritate, ut etiam in hac gratia abundetis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 7." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">raihtis</HI> ] hac particula  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>per</FOREIGN>  encliticum redditur,
sic L. I, 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">unte raihtis</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpeidhvper</FOREIGN> ). XVIII, 14
 <HI REND="ITALIC">þau raihtis</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hæper</FOREIGN> ).— <HI REND="ITALIC">ïn</HI> ] sec. in,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ana</HI> ]
in,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.— <HI REND="ITALIC">friaþvai</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">frijaþvai.</HI></NOTE>  faura dustodida. svah ustiuhai ïn ïzvis jah þo anst. akei sve raihtis ïn allamma managniþ
galaubeinai jah vaurda jah kunþja jah ïn allai usdaudein jah ana þizai us ïzvis ïn uns friaþvai
 <NOTE N="8." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> Non sicut dominans dico vobis, sed propter hanc aliorum sollicitudinem etiam vestrae caritatis sinceritatem
probans.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 8." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">svasve fraujinonds</HI> ] sicut dominans, gr.
omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kat1 ejpitaghvn</FOREIGN> ; Goth. c. Vulg.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvis</HI> ] vobis,
 <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. om.— <HI REND="ITALIC">usdaudeins</HI> ] sic recte cod. A, cod. B †
 <HI REND="ITALIC">usdaudein.—friaþvos</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">frijaþvos.</HI></NOTE>  ei jah ïn þizai anstai managnaiþ. ni svasve fraujinonds qiþa ïzvis ak ïn þizos anþaraize usdaudeins
 <NOTE N="9." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> Nam cognoscitis gratiam domini nostri Jesu Christi, quod propter vos pauperem-fecit se
dives existens, ut vos hac ejus paupertate divites fiatis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 9." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">gabeigai</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">gabigai.</HI></NOTE>  jah ïzvaraizos friaþvos airkniþa kiusands. unte kunnuþ anst fraujins unsaris ïesuis
xristaus þatei ïn ïzvara gaunledida sik gabigs visands ei jus þamma ïs unledja gabeigai vairþaiþ.
 <NOTE N="10." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> Et consilium in hoc do, nam hoc vobis melius
est, vos qui non solum velle, sed etiam facere incepistis a praecedente anno.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 10." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah ragin</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">jar-ragin.—viljan—taujan</HI> ]
¶ cod. A c. gr. omn.; cod. B cum vers. Syr.
et Arab. (ab ea, quam edidit Walton prorsus diversa,
exstante in bibliotheca Ambrosiana in cod. pentaglotto
epistolas Pauli continente.  <ED>CAST.</ED> ), Caeterum
 <COL N="0766"></COL> Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tov</FOREIGN>  utr., sic vs. seq.</NOTE>  jah ragin ïn þamma giba. unte þata ïzvis batizo ïst. juzei ni þatainei viljan ak jah taujan
 <NOTE N="11." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> Verum nunc ecce
etiam facere perficiatis, ut sicut adest animus ad cupiendum, sic etiam ad perficiendum, ex quo habetis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 11." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0766" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0766"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">fauraïst</HI> ] adest,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.— <HI REND="ITALIC">du</HI> ] sec.
ad, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tov</FOREIGN> ; Goth. c. cod. n ap. Mi. et verss. lat.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touð</FOREIGN> 
legit.— <HI REND="ITALIC">habaiþ</HI> ] habetis, cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">habai</HI>  (habeat) c.
vers. Copt.</NOTE>  dugunnuþ af fairnin jera. ïþ nu sai jah taujan ustiuhaiþ ei svasve faura ïst muns du viljan sva jah
 <NOTE N="12." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> Si enim voluntas in parato est, sicut habeat, bene acceptum est, non sicut non habeat.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 12." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0766" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0766"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">vilja</HI> ] sic codd., Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">viljan.—gagreftai</HI> ]
sic Grim. W. J. p. 192 et Gram. III, 514 recte
conjecit  <CITN>(cf. L. II, 1)</CITN>  et Mssm. B. A. p. 325 dicit in
cod. altero ita scriptum esse videri, cum alter hac
parte mutilatus sit; Cast.  <HI REND="ITALIC">gagrei . . . . tai,</HI>  sed  <HI REND="ITALIC">gagreftai</HI> 
ap. Add. p. 67.— <HI REND="ITALIC">svasve</HI> ] Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejavn</FOREIGN>  et paulo post
c. codd.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tiû.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">ïst</HI> ] sec. est,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.</NOTE>  du ustiuhan us þammei habaiþ. jabai auk vilja ïn gagreftai ïst. svasve habai. vaila andanem ïst. ni
 <NOTE N="13." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> Non sic
enim ut aliis quies, verum vobis tristitia, sed ex aequalitate;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 13." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0766" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0766"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">sva</HI> ] sic,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn., nisi Goth.  <HI REND="ITALIC">svaei</HI>  interjecta
 <HI REND="ITALIC">auk</HI>  particula diremit; de simili tmesi vid. ad
L. I, 20.</NOTE> <NOTE N="14." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> in hoc nunc tempore vestra abundantia
ad illorum inopias, ut etiam illorum abundantia fiat ad vestras inopias, ut fiat aequalitas,</NOTE>  svasve ni habai. ni sva auk ei anþaraim ïusila ïþ ïzvis aglo ak us ïbnassau. ïn þamma nu mela ïzvar
ufarassus du jainaize þarbom. ei jah jainaize ufarassus vairþai du ïzvaraim þarbom ei vairþai
 <NOTE N="15." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> sicut
scriptum est: qui multum, non plus et qui paucum, non minus.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 15." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0766" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0766"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">managizo—faviso</HI> ] plus—minus, gr.
omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpleovnase—hjlattovnhse.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">jah saei</HI> ] cod. A
 <HI REND="ITALIC">jas-saei.</HI></NOTE> <NOTE N="16." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0765" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0765"></COL> At gratia Deo, qui dedit hanc
eamdem sollicitudinem pro vobis in cor Titi, nam quidem precem accepit;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="VIII, 16." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0766" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0766"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">aviliud</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">aviliuþ.—ïzei</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïze.—faur
ïzvis</HI> ] cod. B  <SUP>o</SUP>  †.</NOTE>  ïbnassus. svasve gameliþ ïst. saei filu ni managizo jah saei leitil ni favizo. aþþan aviliud guþa. ïzei
