decernitis?</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 20." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0816" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0816"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">þis</HI> ] cod. A pergit.— <HI REND="ITALIC">þanaseiþs</HI> ] adhuc,
 <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.; Goth. c. vers. Arm. Vulg. et Patr.
latt.</NOTE>  vahseiþ du vahstau guþs. jabai gasvultuþ miþ xristau af stabim þis fairwaus. wa þanaseiþs
 <NOTE N="21." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0815" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0815"></COL> Ne tangas, ne adedas, ne gustes,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 21." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0816" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0816"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ni</HI> ] sec et tert., cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">nih.—atsnarpjais—kausjais</HI> ]
¶ gr. omn.</NOTE> <NOTE N="22." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0815" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0815"></COL> quod est omne ad corruptionem, per quod id
adhibeatur secundum praecepta et doctrinas hominum,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 22." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0816" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0816"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">laiseinim</HI> ] sic codd.; Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">laisenim.</HI></NOTE>  sve qivai ïn þamma fairwau urrediþ. ni teikais ni atsnarpjais ni kausjais. þatei ïst all du riurein.
 <NOTE N="23." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0815" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0815"></COL> quae sunt quidem rationem habentia sapientiae
 <COL N="0817"></COL> opinionis in observatione et humilitate cordis et non-temperatione corporis, non in honore aliquo ad saturitatem
carnis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 23." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0816" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0816"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">sveþauh vaurd</HI> ] ¶ gr. omn.— <HI REND="ITALIC">þuhtaus</HI> ]
opinionis,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr., omn.; Goth. hoc additamento perversam
vel ineptam sapientiam indicare voluisse videtur.— <HI REND="ITALIC">fastubnja</HI> ]
 <COL N="0817"></COL> observatione, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejqeloqrhskeiva.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">hairtins</HI> ]
cordis,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.; sunt quidem codd., qui  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touð
noovû</FOREIGN>  addant, sed vid. ad III, 12.— <HI REND="ITALIC">unfreideinai</HI> ] sic
cod. A; cod. B et Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">unfreidei,</HI>  vid. ad Rom.
IX, 30.</NOTE>  þairh þatei ïs brukjaidau bi anabusnim jah laiseinim manne. þoei sind sveþauh vaurd habandona
handugeins þuhtaus ïn fastubnja jah hauneinai hairtins jah unfreideinai leikis ni ïn sveriþo wizai du
 <COL N="0817"></COL> <NOTE N="III, 1." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> Si igitur consurrexistis Christo, quae supra sunt, quaerite, ubi Christus est in dextra
Dei sedens;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 1." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">þarei</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">þar</HI>  (ibi).</NOTE>  soþa leikis. jabai nu miþurrisuþ xristau. þoei ïupa sind sokeiþ. þarei xristus ïst ïn taihsvai guþs sitands.
 <NOTE N="2." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> quae supra sunt, cogitate, non haec quae super terram sunt,</NOTE> <NOTE N="3." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> nam mortui-estis et vita
vestra abscondita est cum Christo in Deo.</NOTE>  þaimei ïupa sind fraþjaiþ ni þaim þoei ana airþai sind. unte gadauþnodeduþ jah libains ïzvara
 <NOTE N="4." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> Cum Christus manifestus fit, vita vestra, tunc etiam vos manifesti
fitis cum eo in gloria.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 4." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvara</HI> ] vestra, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJmwðn.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">þanuh</HI> ] sic
codd., nec B  <HI REND="ITALIC">þannu,</HI>  nec A  <HI REND="ITALIC">þannuh,</HI>  uti Cast.
edidit et adnotavit.— <HI REND="ITALIC">miþ ïmma</HI> ] gr. ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">bairhtai.</HI></NOTE>  gafulgina ïst miþ xristau in guþa. þan xristus svikunþs vairþiþ libains ïzvara. þanuh jah jus bairhtai
 <NOTE N="5." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> Occidite igitur membra vestra haec, quae sunt super terram adulterium,
impuritatem, libidinem, cupiditatem malam et avaritiam, quae est idolorum servitus;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 5." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">horinassu</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">norinassau,</HI>  vid. ad Mc. VII,
32.— <HI REND="ITALIC">vinnon</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">vinna.—ubilana</HI> ] sic recte
cod. A; cod. B †  <HI REND="ITALIC">ubila—sei</HI> ] vid. ad Tim. l, VI,
10.</NOTE>  vairþiþ miþ ïmma ïn vulþau. dauþeiþ nu liþuns ïzvarans þans þaiei sind ana airþai horinassu
 <NOTE N="6." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> per quae venit ira
Dei super filios incredulitatis,</NOTE>  unhrainein vinnon lustu ubilana jah faihugeironi. sei ïst galiugagude skalkinassus. þairh þoei qimiþ
 <NOTE N="7." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> in quibus etiam vos ivistis olim, cum vixistis in his.</NOTE> <NOTE N="8." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> Verum nunc deponite
etiam vos haec omnia: iram, animositatem, improbitatem, convicium, impudicum-sermonem; ex ore
vestro ne exeat.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 8." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">nu</HI> ] vid. ad Rom. VII, 6.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvaramma</HI> ] desinit
cod. A.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ni usgaggai</HI> ] ne exeat,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.
praeter cod. G. Goth. conspirat cum loco parallelo
Eph. IV, 29.</NOTE>  hatis guþs ana sunum ungalaubeinais. ïn þaimei jah jus ïddjeduþ simle. þan libaideduþ ïn þaim. ïþ
nu aflageiþ jah jus þo alla hatis þvairhein unselein anaqiss aglaitivaurdein. us munþa ïzvaramma ni
 <NOTE N="9." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> Ne mentiamini vobis invicem, exuentes vobis hunc antiquum hominem cum factis ejus</NOTE> <NOTE N="10." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> et vestite novo, hoc renovato ad cognitionem secundum imaginem hujus, qui creavit eum.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 10." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">gahamoþ</HI> ] vestite, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejndusavmenoi.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  usgaggai. ni liugaiþ ïzvis misso afslaupjandans ïzvis þana fairnjan mannan miþ tojam ïs jah gahamoþ
 <NOTE N="11." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> Ubi
non-est Graecus et Iudaeus, circumcisio et praeputium, barbarus et Scythus, servus et liber, sed omnia
et in omnibus Christus.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 11." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah</HI> ] tert. et quart. et,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.</NOTE>  niujamma þamma ananividin du ufkunþja bi frisahtai þis saei gaskof ïna. þarei nist kreks jah
ïudaius. bimait jah faurafilli. barbarus jah skyþus. skalks jah freis. ak alla jah ïn allaim xristus.
 <NOTE N="12." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> Induite vobis igitur, ut electi Dei sancti et electi, viscera, commiserationem,
misericordiam, probitatem, humilitatem m(entis), mansuetudinem, patientiam,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 12." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">bleiþein</HI> ] commiserationem, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oijktirmouð</FOREIGN> 
vel  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oijktirmwðn</FOREIGN> ; quod deinde Goth.  <HI REND="ITALIC">armahairtein</HI> 
(misericordiam) addit,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn. et glossam ad verbum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">bleiþein</HI>  in textum illatam esse judicamus.— <HI REND="ITALIC">a . . . </HI> ]
praeter hanc litteram Cast. propter lituram
membranae nihil conspicere potuit; in adnotatione
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ahins</HI>  supplendum esse suspicans, verum tetigisse
 <COL N="0818"></COL> nobis videtur, nam sic  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tapeinofrosuvnh</FOREIGN>  etiam Philip.
II, 3 per  <HI REND="ITALIC">hauneins gahugdais</HI>  et supra II, 23 per  <HI REND="ITALIC">hauneins
hairtins</HI>  convertitur, quorum altero loco codd.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touð noovû</FOREIGN>  additum habent, cui voci, aut si Gothus non
legit, ejus sensui optime respondet, uti  <HI REND="ITALIC">gahugds</HI>  et
 <HI REND="ITALIC">hairto,</HI>  sic  <HI REND="ITALIC">aha,</HI>  vid Philipp. IV, 7; Tit. I, 15.</NOTE>  gahamoþ ïzvis nu sve gavalisai guþs veihans jah valisans brusts bleiþein armahairtein selein haunein
 <NOTE N="13." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> tolerantes vos invicem et
condonantes ipsi; si quis adversus quem habeat querelam, sicut etiam Christus condonavit vobis, sic etiam
vos faciatis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 13." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0818" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0818"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">viþra</HI> ] Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">viþka.—taujaiþ</HI> ] faciatis,
 <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.</NOTE>  a . . . qairrein usbeisnein. þulandans ïzvis misso jah fragibandans silbans. jabai was viþra wana habai
 <NOTE N="14." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> At super omnia amorem, qui est vinculum perfectionis,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 14." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0818" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0818"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">alla</HI> ] Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touvtoiû.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  fairina svasve jah xristus fragaf ïzvis sva jah jus taujaiþ. aþþan ufar alla friaþva. sei ïst gabindi
 <NOTE N="15." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> et pax Dei exsultet in
cordibus vestris, in quo etiam vocati fuistis in uno corpore et grati fiatis;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 15." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0818" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0818"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">guþs</HI> ] Dei, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Cristouð.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">svignjaiþ</HI> ] vid. ad
Thessal. I, IV, 14.</NOTE>  ustauhtais. jah gavairþi guþs svignjaiþ ïn hairtam ïzvaraim. ïn þammei jah laþodai vesuþ ïn ainamma
 <NOTE N="16." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> verbum Christi
habitet in vobis largiter, in omni sapientia et prudentia spirituali docentes et admonentes vos
ipsos psalmis, laudibus, cantibus spiritualibus in gratia canentes in cordibus vestris domino.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 16." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0818" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0818"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jah frodein ahmeinai</HI> ] et prudentia spirituali,
 <SUP>o</SUP>  omn. gr. et verss.; efficitur hoc additamento,
nisi ex alio loco huc translatum est, amplificatio notionis,
cujus figurae exempla ad Cor. I, IX, 25 collegimus;
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ahmeinai</HI>  autem h. l. Goth. ex eodem fonte
hausisse videtur, unde I, 28 codd. graeci et verss.,
quibuscum Goth. fere semper consentire solet,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pneumatikhðé</FOREIGN> 
duxerunt.— <HI REND="ITALIC">psalmom</HI> ] Goth. e. codd. et h. l.
et aute  <HI REND="ITALIC">saggvam</HI>   <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">saggvim</HI> ] sic cod. B Cast. †
 <HI REND="ITALIC">saggvam,</HI>  sed postea  <HI REND="ITALIC">saggvim</HI>  Add. p. 70.— <HI REND="ITALIC">fraujin</HI> ]
domino, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qewðé.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  leika jah aviliudondans vairþaiþ. vaurd xristaus bauai ïn ïzvis gabigaba. ïn allai handugein
jah frodein ahmeinai laisjandans jah talzjandans ïzvis silbans psalmom hazeinim saggvim
 <NOTE N="17." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> Omne quodcumque quod faciatis in verbo aut in opere, omne in nomine domini Iesu gratificantes
Deo patri per eum.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 17." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0818" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0818"></COL> init. et deinde post  <HI REND="ITALIC">guþa</HI>  Goth. c. codd.
 <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  ahmeinaim ïn anstai siggvandans ïn hairtam ïzvaraim fraujin. all þiswah þatei taujaiþ ïn
vaurda aiþþau ïn vaurstva. all ïn namin fraujins ïesuis aviliudondans guþa attin þairh
 <NOTE N="18." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> Vos uxores, pareatis viris vestris, ut convenit in domino;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 18." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0818" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0818"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">jus</HI> ] vos, vid. ad L. VI, 20.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvaraim</HI> ] vestris,
 <SUP>o</SUP>  gr., cf. ad Cor. I, VII, 16.</NOTE> <NOTE N="19." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0817" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0817"></COL> viri, amate
 <COL N="0819"></COL> uxores vestras et ne sitis acerbi contra has;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 19." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0818" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0818"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvaros</HI> ] vestras,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.</NOTE>  ïna. jus qinons ufhausjaiþ vairam ïzvaraim sve gaqimiþ ïn fraujin. vairos frijoþ qenins
 <COL N="0819"></COL> <NOTE N="20." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> filii, pareatis parentibus secundum omne, nam hoc
bene placitum est in domino;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 20." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïst</HI> ] gr. ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">vaila.</HI></NOTE>  ïzvaros jah ni sijaiþ baitrai viþra þos. barna ufhausjaiþ fadreinam bi all. unte þata vaila
 <NOTE N="21." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> vos patres, ne sollicitetis filios vestros ad animositatem, ut non fiant
in aegritudine;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 21." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">du þvairhein</HI> ] errat Cast. dicens  <HI REND="ITALIC">du þvairhein</HI> 
superfluum esse, quia  <HI REND="ITALIC">gramjan</HI>  proprie  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejreqivzein</FOREIGN> 
significet; nam quod additum est  <HI REND="ITALIC">du þvairhein</HI>  (ad
iram) verbo  <HI REND="ITALIC">gramjan</HI>  (sollicitare), eo comprobatur
Goth. non  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejreqivzete,</FOREIGN>  sed c. codd.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parorgivzete</FOREIGN>  legisse.</NOTE>  galekaiþ ïst ïn fraujin. jus attans ni gramjaiþ barna ïzvara du þvairhein ei ni vairþaina
 <NOTE N="22." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> servi, pareatis secundum omne corpore dominis, non in oculis servientes, ut hominibus
placentes, sed in simplicitate cordis timentes Deum.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 22." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">leika fraujam</HI> ] Cast. † jct., nam  <HI REND="ITALIC">leika</HI>  respondet
graeco  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kataú savrka</FOREIGN>  quod quidem addita  <HI REND="ITALIC">bi</HI> 
praepositione reddendum erat, et aegre etiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">þaim</HI> 
articulum desideramus ( <HI REND="ITALIC">þaim bi leika fraujam).—guþ</HI> ]
Deum, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kuvrion.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  ïn unlustau. þevisa ufhausjaiþ bi all leika fraujam ni ïn augam skalkinondans sve mannam samjandans
 <NOTE N="23." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> Quodcumque quod faciatis, ex animo operemini
ut domino, non hominibus,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 23." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> init. Goth. c. codd.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú paðn.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">fraujin</HI> ]
Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  ak ïn ainfalþein hairtins ogandans guþ. þiswah þatei taujaiþ us saivalai vaurkjaiþ sve fraujin
 <NOTE N="24." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> scientes, quod a domino accipitis mercedem haereditatis, nam domino
Christo servitis.</NOTE> <NOTE N="25." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> Hic enim noxius accipit quod nocuit, et non - est favor apud Deum.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 25." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">auk</HI> ] enim, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">viljahalþei</HI> ] cod. B et
Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">viljahalþein,</HI>  vid. Eph. VI, 9.— <HI REND="ITALIC">at guþa</HI> ]
apud Deum,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.</NOTE>  ni mannam vitandans þatei af fraujin nimiþ andalauni arbjis. unte fraujin xristau skalkinoþ. sa auk
 <NOTE N="IV, 1." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> Vos
domini justitiam et aequitatem servis praestate, scientes quod habetis etiam vos dominum in coelis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 1." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">aihuþ</HI> ] gr. omn. post  <HI REND="ITALIC">jus.</HI></NOTE>  skaþula andnimiþ þatei skoþ jah nist viljahalþei at guþa. jus fraujans garaiht jah ïbnassu þevisam
 <NOTE N="2." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> Rogationi
adjungentes vos, vigilantes in ea in gratibus:</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 2." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">haftjandans</HI> ] adjungentes, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>proskartereiðte,</FOREIGN> 
praeter cod. Colb. 7 ap. Mill.— <HI REND="ITALIC">aviliudam</HI> ]
gratibus, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujcaristivaé.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  atkunnaiþ vitandans þatei aihuþ jah jus fraujan ïn himinam. bidai haftjandans ïzvis vakandans ïn
 <NOTE N="3." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> rogantes simul etiam pro nobis, ut Deus aperiat
nobis ostium verbi ad dicendum mysterium Christi, propter quod etiam vinctus sum,</NOTE>  ïzai ïn aviliudam. bidjandans samana jah bi uns ei guþ uslukai unsis haurd vaurdis du rodjan runa
 <NOTE N="4." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> ut manifestem
hoc, sicuti debeam loqui;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 4." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">svasve</HI> ] pergit cod. A.</NOTE> <NOTE N="5." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> in sapientia eatis ad hoc foris, hoc tempus redimentes.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 5." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">þata</HI> ]  <SUP>o</SUP>  cod. A.</NOTE>  xristaus ïn pizozei jah gabundans ïm. ei gabairhtjau þo svasve skuljau rodjan. ïn handugein gaggaiþ
 <NOTE N="6." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> Verbum vestrum
semper in gratia sale conditum sit, ut sciatis quomodo debeatis unicuique respondere.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 6." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvar</HI> ] Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvak.—gasuqoþ</HI> ] sic codd.,
nec cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">gasukoþ,</HI>  uti Cast. adnotavit; in cod.
 <COL N="0820"></COL> Arg. bis  <CITN>(Mc. IX, 50; L. XIV, 34)</CITN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">gasupon</HI>  eodem
sensu legitur.— <HI REND="ITALIC">siai</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">sijai,</HI>  quod gr. omn.
omittunt.— <HI REND="ITALIC">ei viteiþ</HI> ] ut sciatis, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijdevnai</FOREIGN> ;
Goth. c. Vulg.</NOTE>  du þaim uta þata mel usbugjandans. vaurd ïzvar sinteino ïn anstai salta gasuqoþ siai ei viteiþ waiva
 <NOTE N="7." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> Quod
secundum me est, omne notificat vobis Tycecus, hic carus frater et fidus minister et conservitium in domino,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 7." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0820" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0820"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">tykekus</HI> ] cod. A  <HI REND="ITALIC">tykeikus.</HI></NOTE>  skuleiþ ainwarjammeh andhafjan. þatei bi mik ïst all gakanneiþ ïzvis tykekus sa liuba broþar jah
 <NOTE N="8." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> quem misi ad vos ideo, ut cognoscat quid de vobis est, et consoletur corda vestra,</NOTE>  triggva andbahts jah gaskalki ïn fraujin. þanei ïnsandida du ïzvis duþþe ei kunnjai wa bi ïzvis ïst
 <NOTE N="9." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> cum
Onisimo, hoc caro et fido fratre, qui est e vobis, qui omne vobis notificant, quod hic est.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 9." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0820" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0820"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">liubin—triggvin</HI> ] ¶ gr.— <HI REND="ITALIC">þaiei</HI> ] qui,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.;
Goth. c. cod. D  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiå.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  jah gaþrafstjai hairtona ïzvara miþ aunisimau þamma liubin jah triggvin broþr. saei ïst us ïzvis.
 <NOTE N="10." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> Salutat
vos Aristarcus, hic concaptivus mihi et Marcus, consobrinus Barnabae, de quo accepistis mandata, si
veniat ad vos, accipiatis eum;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 10." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0820" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0820"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">areistarkus</HI> ] cod. A †  <HI REND="ITALIC">ariastarkus.—du</HI> ]
notandus est novus usus hujus praepositionis, cum
accusativo positae, praeter hunc locum etiam vs. 13;
valet autem utroque loco idem quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">bi</HI>  (pro),
quapropter ii loci non ad confirmandam opinionem
afferri possunt, etiam J. XVI, 32  <HI REND="ITALIC">seina</HI>  accusativum a
 <HI REND="ITALIC">du</HI>  pendentem esse; ad illum enim locum haec
significatio non pertinet.</NOTE>  þaiei all ïzvis gakannjand þatei her ïst. goleiþ ïzvis areistarkus sa miþfrahunþana mis jah markus
 <NOTE N="11." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> et Iesus, qui vocatur Justus, qui sunt e circumcisione. Hi uni cooperatores
sunt regni Dei, qui fuerunt mihi ad consolationem.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 11." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0820" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0820"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">sind</HI> ] sunt,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.— <HI REND="ITALIC">þiudangardjos</HI> ] regni,
gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû thún basileivan.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  gadiliggs barnabins. du þanei nemuþ anabusnins. jabai qimai at ïzvis. andnimaiþ ïna. jah ïesus saei
haitada justus þaiei sind us bimaita. þai ainai gavaurstvans sind þiudangardjos guþs. þaiei vesun mis
 <NOTE N="12." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> Salutat vos Epafras, hic e vobis servus
Christi, hic semper certans de vobis in precibus, ut stetis omnoperantes et perfecti in omni voluntate
Dei;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 12." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0820" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0820"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">sa</HI> ] sec. hic,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.— <HI REND="ITALIC">allavaurstvans—fullavitans</HI> ]
¶ gr. omn. et Goth. c. codd.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>peplhroforhmevnoi</FOREIGN> 
pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>peplhrwmevnoi</FOREIGN>  legit.</NOTE>  du gaþrafsteinai. goleiþ ïzvis aipafras sa us izvis skalks xristaus sa sinteino usdaudjands bi ïzvis ïn
 <NOTE N="13." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> testor enim ei, quod habet multum studium pro vobis et de his qui sunt in Laudicea et Ieropola.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 13." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0820" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0820"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">manag aljan</HI> ] multam aemulationem, gr.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>poluún povnon.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">du</HI> ] pro,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.; caeterum vid. ad
vs. 10.— <HI REND="ITALIC">sind</HI> ] desinit cod. A.— <HI REND="ITALIC">jah</HI> ] sec. Goth.
 <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>twðn ejn.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  bidom ei standaiþ allavaurstvans jah fullavitans ïn allamma viljin guþs. veitvodja auk ïmma þatei
 <NOTE N="14." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> Salutat vos Lucas, medicus hic carus;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 14." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0820" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0820"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">liuba</HI> ] Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú Dhmaðû.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  habaiþ manag aljan bi ïzvis jah du þans þaiei sind ïn laudeikaia jah ïairaupaulein. goleiþ ïzvis lukas
 <NOTE N="15." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0819" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0819"></COL> salutate hos in Laudicea fratres et Nymfan et hanc
 <COL N="0821"></COL> inquilinam ejus ecclesiam.</NOTE>  leikeis sa liuba. goleiþ þans ïn laudeikaia broþruns jah nymfan jah þo ïngardjon ïs aikklesjon.
 <COL N="0821"></COL> <NOTE N="16." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> Et cum legatur apud vos haec epistola, faciatis, ut etiam in Laudecea
ecclesia legatur, et quae est e Laudicea, vos legatis,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 16." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">laudekaion</HI> ] sic scribendum est pro mendosa
codicis B lectione  <HI REND="ITALIC">laudekaiom.—þoei</HI> ] nisi sic errore
librarii pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">soei</HI>  (i. q.  <HI REND="ITALIC">sei</HI> ) scripta est, div.  <HI REND="ITALIC">þo ei</HI> 
(hanc quae) legendum, vid. ad L. I, 20.— <HI REND="ITALIC">laudeikaion</HI> ]
sec. Goth. c. Vulg.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iåna kaiv.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">ussiggvaid. jah</HI> ] cod.
B et Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">ussiggvaidjau.</HI></NOTE>  jah þan ussiggvaidau at ïzvis so aipistaule. taujaiþ ei jah ïn laudekaion aikklesjon ussiggvaidau jah
 <NOTE N="17." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> et dicatis Arcippo: vide hoc ministerium quod
accepisti in domino, ut id impleas.</NOTE>  þoei ïst us laudeikaion jus ussiggvaid. jah qiþaiþ arkippau saiw þata andbahti þatei andnamt ïn
 <NOTE N="18." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> Salutatio mea manu Pavli.</NOTE> <NOTE N="19." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> Mementote mei vinculi. Gratia
cum vobis amen.

 <CAPTION COM="0821">Ad Colossenses explicit.</CAPTION></NOTE>   <NOTE N="IV, 19." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0822" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0822"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">bandjos</HI> ] vinculi, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>desmwðn.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">amen</HI> ]
amen,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.

Subscriptio. Nullus gr. eam uti Goth. habet;
caeterum pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">kaulaussaim</HI>  in cod. per compendium
 <HI REND="ITALIC">kaussaim</HI>  scriptum est.</NOTE>  fraujin ei ïta usfulljais. goleins meinai handau pavlaus. gamuneiþ meinaizos bandjos. ants miþ ïzvis
amen.</P> <CAPTION COM="0821">du kaulaussaim ustauh</CAPTION></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0821" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0821">DU þAISSALAUNEIKIM. ·A· <NOTE TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=N COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> <P COM="0821">Fragmenta hujus epistolae in cod. B leguntur;
cod. A inde a V, 22 usque ad finem solummodo
habet.</P> 

 <P COM="0821">Inscriptionem supplevimus e Philipp. IV, 16, ubi
 <HI REND="ITALIC">þaissalauneika,</HI>  Thessalonices oppidi nomen invenitur.</P></NOTE></HEAD> <COL N="0821"></COL> <P COM="0821"><NOTE N="II, 10." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> ——et Deus, quam sancte et juste et irreprehensibiliter vobis his credentibus fuimus,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 10." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">waiva</HI> ] quam ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pwðû</FOREIGN> ), gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wJû.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">veihaba</HI> ]
sancte, Goth. fortasse c. cod. F  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aJgivwû</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJsivwû</FOREIGN>  legit,
nam  <HI REND="ITALIC">veihs</HI>  graeco  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aågioû</FOREIGN>  respondet, vid. tamen Tit. I,
8, ubi quoque pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåsioû</FOREIGN>  ponitur.</NOTE> —jah guþ waiva veihaba jah garaihtaba jah unfairinodaba ïzvis þaim galaubjandam vesum.
 <NOTE N="11." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> sicut
scitis unumquemque vestrum, uti pater filios suos rogantes vos et consolantes</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 11." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">vituþ</HI> ] Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wJû (pwðû</FOREIGN> ).</NOTE> <NOTE N="12." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> et testantes ad eundum
vos digne Deo, qui vocavit vos ad suum regnum et gloriam.</NOTE>  svasve vituþ ainwarjanoh ïzvara sve atta barna seina bidjandans ïzvis jah gaþlaihandans jah veitvodjandans
 <NOTE N="13." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> Ideo etiam nos gratias agimus Deo indesinenter,
nam accipientes a nobis verbum auditus Dei accepistis non sicuti verbum hominum, sed sicuti est
vere verbum Dei, quod etiam operatur in vobis, vos - qui creditis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 13." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">unsveibandans</HI> ] sic cod. B; Cast. Add. p. 71.— <HI REND="ITALIC">at
unst</HI> ] gr. omn. post  <HI REND="ITALIC">hauseinais;</HI>  Goth. c. Vulg.— <HI REND="ITALIC">svasve</HI> ]
pr.,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.; Goth. c. verss.— <HI REND="ITALIC">vaurkeiþ</HI> ] sic
 <COL N="0822"></COL> scribendum est pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">vaurkei,</HI>  codicis B et Cast. lectione.</NOTE>  du gaggan ïzvis vairþaba guþs. saei laþoda ïzvis du seinai þiudangardjai jah vulþau. duþe
jah veis aviliudom guþa unsveibandans. unte nimandans at uns vaurd hauseinais guþs andnemuþ ni
svasve vaurd manne ak svasve ïst sunjaba vaurd guþs. þatei jah vaurkheiþ ïn izvis juzei galaubeiþ.
 <NOTE N="14." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> Vos enim imitatores facti - estis,
fratres, ecclesiis Dei his exsistentibus in Iudaea in Christo Iesu; nam hoc idem passi estis etiam vos a vestris
popularibus, sicuti etiam nos ab Iudaeis,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 14." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0822" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0822"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">veis</HI> ] nos, gr. omn.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtoiv.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  jus auk galeikondans vaurþuþ broþrjus aikklesjom guþs þaim visandeim ïn ïudaia ïn xristau ïesu.
 <NOTE N="15." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> qui etiam dominum occiderunt Iesum et proprios profetas
et nos persecuti-sunt et Deo non placentes et omnibus hominibus adversarii sunt,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 15." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0822" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0822"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">svesaim</HI> ] proprios, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touvû.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  unte þata samo vunnuþ jah jus fram ïzvaraim ïnkunjam svasve jah veis fram ïudaium. þaiei jah
fraujin usqemun ïesua jah svesaim praufetum jah uns fravrekun jah guþa ni galeikandans jah allaim
 <NOTE N="16." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> arcentes nos ad gentiles
loqui, ut servarentur, ad explendum sua peccata semper. At properavit super eos ira Dei usque finem.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 16." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0822" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0822"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">guþs</HI> ] dei,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr.</NOTE>  mannam andaneiþans sind. varjandans uns du þiudom rodjan ei ganisaina du usfulljan seinos fravaurhtins
 <NOTE N="17." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> At nos, fratres, orbati a vobis ad tempus horae, facie non corde abundantia properavimus vultum vestrum
conspicere in multa cupiditate.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 17." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0822" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0822"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvara</HI> ] ad  <HI REND="ITALIC">andaugi</HI>  pertinens soloece pro
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvar</HI>  dictum est; pro genitivo plurali haberi, sermonis
gothici usus vetat.</NOTE>  sinteino. aþþan snauh ana ïns hatis guþs und andi. aþþan veis broþrjus gaainanaidai af ïzvis
du mela weilos andvairþja ni hairtin ufarassau sniumidedum andaugi ïzvara gasaiwan ïn managamma
 <NOTE N="18." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> Nam voluimus venire ad vos ego quidem Pavlus et una vice et duabus,
et impedivit nos Satana.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 18." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0822" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0822"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">unte</HI> ] nam, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>diov.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  lustau. unte vildedum qimam at ïzvis ïk raihtis pavlus jah ainamma sinþa jah tvaim jah analatida uns
 <NOTE N="19." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0821" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0821"></COL> Quid enim est nostra spes aut gaudium aut corona gloriationis? Nonne
 <COL N="0823"></COL> vos in facie domini nostri Iesu Christi in ejus adventu?</NOTE>   <NOTE N="II, 19." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0822" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0822"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ïst</HI> ] est,  <SUP>o</SUP>  gr. omn.— <HI REND="ITALIC">niu</HI> ] nonne, gr. omn.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ oujciú kaiv</FOREIGN> ; Goth. c. Vulg.</NOTE>  satana. wa auk ist unsara vens aiþþau faheþs aiþþau vaips woftuljos. niu jus ïn andvairþja fraujins
 <COL N="0823"></COL> <NOTE N="20." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> Vos enim estis gloria nostra et gaudium.</NOTE> <NOTE N="III, 1." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> Propter quod non sustinentes amplius placuit nobis, ut relicti essemus in Athenis soli;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 1." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0822" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0822"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ju—þanamais</HI> ] de hac loquendi ubertate vid.
ad L. XV, 19, sufficiebat enim  <HI REND="ITALIC">ju ni</HI>  ad reddendum
graecum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mhkevti,</FOREIGN>  vid. vs. 5.</NOTE>  unsaris ïesuis xristaus ïn ïs quma. jus auk siuþ vulþus unsar jah faheþs. ïn þizei ju ni usþulandans
 <NOTE N="2." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> et misimus
Timotheum, fratrem nostrum et ministrum Dei in evangelio Christi, ut vos confirmaret et oraret
secundum fidem vestram,</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 2." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">andbaht</HI> ] ministrum, gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sunergovn.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">ïz is
gatulgjai</HI> ] ¶ gr. omn.— <HI REND="ITALIC">bidjai</HI> ] Goth. c. codd.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJmaðû.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  þanamais galeikaida uns ei biliþanai veseima ïn aþeinim ainai. jah ïnsandidedum teimauþaiu broþar
unsarana jah andbaht guþs ïn aivaggeljon xristaus ei ïzvis gatulgjai jah bidjai bi galaubein ïzvara.
 <NOTE N="3." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> ut non ullus absterreatur in his angustiis, ipsi enim scitis quod ad hoc
constituti sumus.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 3." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ratidai</HI> ] Cast. sine ullo dubio recte  <HI REND="ITALIC">satidai</HI> 
conjecit, vid. Philipp. I, 17, ubi Goth. pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>keiðmai</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">gasatiþs ïm</HI>  quoque utitur.</NOTE> <NOTE N="4." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> Et enim cum fuimus apud vos, praediximus vobis quod futurum fuit nobis ad patiendum
afflictiones, sicuti etiam factum - est, et scitis.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 4." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">vesum</HI> ] gr. omn. post  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvis.</HI></NOTE>  ei ni ainshun afagjaidau ïn þaim aggviþom. silbans auk. vituþ þatei du þamma ratidai sijum. jah
auk þan vesum at ïzvis. fauraqeþum ïzvis þatei anavairþ vas uns du vinnan agliþos svasve jah varþ
 <NOTE N="5." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> Ideo etiam ego jam non sustinens misi ad cognoscendam
fidem vestram, ne forte tentaverit vos hic tentans et frustra fiat labor noster.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 5." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">usþulands</HI> ] cod. B et Cast. †  <HI REND="ITALIC">usþulans,</HI>  vid.
ad Mc. XII, 24.</NOTE>  jah vituþ. duþþe jah ïk ju ni usþulands ïnsandida du ufkunnan galaubein ïzvara ïbai aufto usfaifraisi
 <NOTE N="6." TYPE="Interpretatio" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> At nunc in
veniente Timotheo ad nos a vobis et narrante nobis fidem, amorem vestrum et quod memoriam nostram
habetis bonam semper, cupientes nos videre, sicuti etiam nos vos;</NOTE>   <NOTE N="III, 6." TYPE="Annotationes" ANCHORED=Y COM="0823" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0823"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">teimauþaiu</HI> ] pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">teimauþaiau,</HI>  vid. ad L. I,
54.— <HI REND="ITALIC">galaubein</HI> ] Goth.  <SUP>o</SUP>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv.</FOREIGN> — <HI REND="ITALIC">habaiþ</HI> ] gr. omn.
ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">gaminþi.</HI></NOTE>  ïzvis sa fraisands jah svare vairþai arbaiþs unsara. aþþan nu at quimandin teimauþaiu at unsis fram
