quod reipsa existit, aut existere affirmatur.</P> <CAPTION COM="1050">1) In simplicibus sententiis:</CAPTION> <P COM="1050"><HI REND="ITALIC">a</HI> ) Mc. XVI, 6  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïesus nist her, urrais:</HI></P> <P COM="1050"><HI REND="ITALIC">b</HI> ) In directa interrogatione: Gal. III, 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">was ïzvis
afhugida?</HI>  Joan. XIII, 36  <HI REND="ITALIC">frauja wad gaggis?</HI></P> <P COM="1050">«Annotatio 1.—In directis interrogationibus ponitur
etiam conjunctivus, vid. § 185, I,  <HI REND="ITALIC">f.</HI></P> <P COM="1050">«Annotatio 2.—Verba  <HI REND="ITALIC">debere,</HI>  oportere (germ.  <HI REND="ITALIC">sollen</HI> )
et velle, more graeco et latino ponuntur in indicativo
