 <HI REND="ITALIC">praizbytaireis</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>presbuvteroû</FOREIGN> ) et  <HI REND="ITALIC">praisbytairei</HI>  (presbyteratus).</P> <CAPTION COM="1067">§ 192. II. De  <HI REND="ITALIC">numero</HI>  hoc est animadvertendum:</CAPTION> <P COM="1067">1) Quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">pluralia tantum</HI>  sint:  <HI REND="ITALIC">berusjos</HI>  majores,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">broþrahans</HI>  fratres ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajdelfoiv</FOREIGN> );  <HI REND="ITALIC">brusts</HI>  pectus, viscera,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">hairþra</HI>  viscera;  <HI REND="ITALIC">bokos</HI>  litterae, epistola;  <HI REND="ITALIC">sarva</HI>  et
 <HI REND="ITALIC">vepna</HI>  arma,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vegos</HI>  fluctus;  <HI REND="ITALIC">daurons</HI>  (vulvae) porta,
fores;  <HI REND="ITALIC">saliþvos</HI>  diversorium,  <HI REND="ITALIC">hlaivasnos</HI>  sepulcretum,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">veinatriva</HI>  vinetum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">laubos</HI>  frondes. Econtrario Gothus
concreta plur. graeca abstractis sing. exhibet,
ut  <HI REND="ITALIC">skufts</HI>  coma pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>trivceû</FOREIGN>  capilli. Sententias autem,
