þizos auþjons mais þau þizos aigandeins aban.</HI></P> <P COM="1085">«Annotatio 1.—Imo etiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">mais</HI>  corroborativum
comparativo ipso conjungitur: Mth. VI, 26  <HI REND="ITALIC">niu jus
mais vulþrizans</HI> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1085" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1085"></COL> Quod haec praeferenda sit lectio pro ea consueta,
a Schmellerio ( <HI REND="ITALIC">Gloss. Hell.</HI>  v.  <HI REND="ITALIC">uhta</HI> ), licet posterius,
 <COL N="1086"></COL> et Halbersma conjecta, ad Mth. VI, 26; Gal. II, 6
diximus.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sijuþ</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>maðllon diafevrete</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">þaim?</HI> 
Cor. II, VIII, 22  <HI REND="ITALIC">broþar gakausidedum filaus mais usdaudozan</HI> 
(simpliciter  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>poluú spoudaiovteron</FOREIGN> ); Phil.
I, 23  <HI REND="ITALIC">lustu haba miþ xristau visan, und filu mais batizo</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>maðllon kreiðsson</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïst.</HI>  E contrario dicitur Mc. V,
26  <HI REND="ITALIC">ni vaihtai botida mais vairs habaida</HI>  non quoquam
