hJmevran</FOREIGN> ); Mc. XIV, 49  <HI REND="ITALIC">daga wammeh</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaq1 hJmevran</FOREIGN> );
Luc. XVI, 19; XIX, 47; Cor. I, XV, 31; Luc. II, 14
 <HI REND="ITALIC">jera wammeh</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kat1 eætoû</FOREIGN> ); Luc. IX, 23  <HI REND="ITALIC">dag wanoh</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaq1 hJmevran</FOREIGN> ); Mth. XXVII, 15  <HI REND="ITALIC">and dulþ warjanoh;</HI> 
Mc. XV, 6.</P> <P COM="1113">« <HI REND="ITALIC">Wazuh</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">warjizuh</HI>  adjectis numeralibus voçabulis
efformant distributiva, vid. § 198, III.</P> <P COM="1113">«Annotatio 10.—Ubi relativa  <HI REND="ITALIC">saei, ïzei, ei, þei</HI> 
sequuntur  <HI REND="ITALIC">wazuh,</HI>  huic praefigitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">sa</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">þis,</HI>  posterius
imprimis ad convertendum Graecum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæn,</FOREIGN>  hinc:
Mth. X, 32, 33  <HI REND="ITALIC">sawazuh saei</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paðû oåstiû</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">andhaitiþ
mis ïn andvairþja manna, andhaita jah ïk imma
ïn andvairþja attins· meinis ïþ þiswanoh saei</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåstiû
aæn,</FOREIGN>  omnis qui)  <HI REND="ITALIC">afaikiþ mik—afaika jah ïk ïna;</HI> 
Mc. XI, 23  <HI REND="ITALIC">þiswazuh ei</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oÝû aæn</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">qiþai·—vairþiþ
ïmma þiswah þei</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oÝ ejavn</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">qiþiþ; 24 allata þiswah
þei</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavnta oåsa aæn</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">bidjandans sokeiþ, vairþiþ
ïzvis;</HI>  Joan. XVI, 2  <HI REND="ITALIC">qimiþ weila ei sawazuh ïzei
usqimiþ</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paðû oJ ajpokteivnaû</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvis, þuggkeiþ hunsla saljan
guþa.</HI>  Attamen etiam legitur apud Joan. XVI, 15
 <HI REND="ITALIC">þatawah þei</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oÝ, ti aån</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">bidjaiþ attan, gibaiþ ïzvis.</HI> 
Alia exempla vid. gloss. h. v.</P> <P COM="1113">«Sed contra ad strictiorem unionem emphatice exprimendam
iisdem  <HI REND="ITALIC">warjizuh</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">waþaruh</HI>  etiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">ain</HI>  praefigitur
