gasatida liþuns ainwarjanoh</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eÝn eåkaston</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïze ïn
leika svasve vilda;</HI>  Skeir. VII, c  <HI REND="ITALIC">svaei ainwarjano</HI> <NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1114" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1114"></COL> Sic enim in codice legitur, uti nobis scripsit
Castillionaeus, pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">ainwarjanoh,</HI>  quod conjeceramus,
et  <HI REND="ITALIC">ainwarjamma,</HI>  legente Massmanno.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">sva filu sve vilda andniman ïs gatavida.</HI>  Commistum
est autem in Cor. I, VII, 17  <HI REND="ITALIC">ni ei warjammeh
svasve gadailida guþ, ainwarjatoh</HI> <NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1114" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1114"></COL> Sic legendum est secundum Castill. Add. p. 66,
non autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">ainwarjizoh,</HI>  uti nos juxta ejusdem Castillionaei
