praeeunte Graeco  <CITN>(ut Phil. II, 22)</CITN> ; primitus enim
praepositio e verbo separata nomini praeponebatur:
Mc. V, 37  <HI REND="ITALIC">miþ mis afargaggan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sunakolouqhðsai
aujtwðé</FOREIGN> ); VIII, 2  <HI REND="ITALIC">miþ mis vesun</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>proûmevnousiv moi</FOREIGN> );
IX, 14  <HI REND="ITALIC">sokjan miþ ïmma</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>suzhéteiðn aujtwðé</FOREIGN> ); IX, 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">rodjan
miþ ïesua</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sullaleiðn twðé 1Ihsouð</FOREIGN> ). Sic etiam Luc. XV, 6
