( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gegenhðsqai</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">bimaitis ïþ þiudos hauhjan guþ.</HI></P> <P COM="1180">«Annotatio 3.—Saepe etiam in gothico sermone
sicut et in germanico verbale objectum per  <HI REND="ITALIC">ei</HI>  vel
 <HI REND="ITALIC">þatei</HI>  circumscribitur, vid. §§ 275, 276.»</P> <P COM="1180">§ 254. Supinum et gerundium Gothus non novit,
et utrumque per infinitivum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">du</HI>  communiter praeposito,
exponit.</P> <CAPTION COM="1180">I. Jamvero ad significandum supinum adhibetur</CAPTION> <P COM="1180">1) Simplex infinitivus, praecipue post verba motus,
vel motum indicantia <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="1179" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1179"></COL> In germanico sermone per  <HI REND="ITALIC">zu, um zu,</HI>  gall. pour, et infinitivum.  <ED><HI REND="ITALIC">Interpr.</HI></ED></NOTE> : Luc. I, 76  <HI REND="ITALIC">fauragaggis
faura andvairþja fraujins manvjan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eJtoimavsai</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">vigans
ïmma;</HI>  Tim. I, I, 15  <HI REND="ITALIC">xristus qam ïn þamma
fairwau fravaurhtans nasjan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>swðsai</FOREIGN> ); Thess. I, II, 17
 <HI REND="ITALIC">sniumidedum andaugi ïzvara gasaiwan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ijdeiðn</FOREIGN> );
Tim. II, IV, 9; Luc. I, 79  <HI REND="ITALIC">gaveisoþ unsara urruns
us hauhiþai gabairhtjan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpifaðnai</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">þaim ïn riqiza;</HI> 
II, 22  <HI REND="ITALIC">brahtedun barn ïn ïairusalem atsatjan</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parasthðsai</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">faura fraujin;</HI>  et etiam alias: Eph. VI,
19  <HI REND="ITALIC">mis gibaidau vaurd ïn balþein kannjan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gnwrivsai</FOREIGN> )
 <HI REND="ITALIC">runa aivaggeljons;</HI>  I, 9, 10.</P> <P COM="1180">2) Communius autem praeposito  <HI REND="ITALIC">du:</HI>  Luc. IV, 18
 <HI REND="ITALIC">frauja ïnsandida mik du ganasjan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ijavsasqai</FOREIGN> )
