Joan. XIV, 3, 21 (XV, 27); XVI, 22; XVIII, 18; Luc.
VIII, 23  <HI REND="ITALIC">þaruh þan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">sve faridedun;</HI>  I, 26  <HI REND="ITALIC">þanuh
þan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïn menoþ saihstin;</HI>  Mth. IX, 17  <HI REND="ITALIC">biþeh
þan</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">jah vein usgutniþ</HI>  Mth. XXVII, 46  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïþ þan</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">bi weila niundon;</HI>  Luc. XVII, 15  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïþ ains þan</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïze,</HI>  vid. § 260, annot. 2; Mc. VI, 17  <HI REND="ITALIC">sa auk
raihtis</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gavr</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">herodes gahabaida ïohanne;</HI>  IX, 41  <HI REND="ITALIC">saei
auk allis</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gavr</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">gadragkjai ïzvis;</HI>  Joan. VIII, 42  <HI REND="ITALIC">nih
þan auk</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gavr</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">fram mis silbin ni qam;</HI>  XII, 10; Luc.
XIX, 27  <HI REND="ITALIC">aþþan sveþauh</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>plhún</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">fijands meinans
briggiþ her,</HI>  vid. § 260, annot. 4; Cor. II, XI, 21
 <HI REND="ITALIC">qiþa sve þatei</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wJû oåti</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">veis siukai sijaima.</HI>  Frequenter
 <COL N="1225"></COL> imprimis occurrit  <HI REND="ITALIC">svaei nu</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wåste</FOREIGN> ) Cor. I,
XIV, 22; XV, 58; II, IV, 12; Phil. IV, 1; Thess. I
IV, 18.</P> <P COM="1225">3) Non tam pleonastice quam potius ad generaliores
textus graeci expressiones determinandas vel
alias perficiendas et amplificandas quandoque adjiciuntur
praedicata, copulativae sententiae, etc.: Mth
