 <HI REND="ITALIC">an,</HI>  vet. sup. germ.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ana,</HI>  suec.  <HI REND="ITALIC">å,</HI>  angl.  <HI REND="ITALIC">on,</HI>  rec. sup.
germ.  <HI REND="ITALIC">an,</HI>  gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnav</FOREIGN> ; Gr. III, 252; Gf. I, 273; Alth.
Praep. 68 sqq.; Rchth. 602). Praepositio accusativum
et dativum regens, graeco  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiú</FOREIGN>  respondens, proprieque
indicans directionem ad locum determinatum,
ita ut hunc inter et subjectum vel objectum jam exoriatur
relatio magis minusve stricta, saltem proximiae;
significat igitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">super</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiv</FOREIGN> ),  <HI REND="ITALIC">ad</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû</FOREIGN> ). Habet insuper
significationem adversativam,  <HI REND="ITALIC">contra, adversus</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katav</FOREIGN>  cum gen.) et causativam,  <HI REND="ITALIC">propter, quod.</HI>  Ad
 <HI REND="ITALIC">tempus</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">modum</HI>  relata haec praepositio non nisi raro
occurrit.</ITEM> <ITEM>I.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Praepositio.</HI>  A. Cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">accusativo:</HI>  1) ad indicandum
