per  <HI REND="ITALIC">afar</HI>   <CITN>(Mc. II, 1)</CITN>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">bi</HI>   <CITN>(Gal. II, 1)</CITN>  convertitur.</ITEM> <ITEM>II. In  <HI REND="ITALIC">compositione</HI>  autem non nisi raro occurrit,
ubi graeco  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dia . . . ,</FOREIGN>  quandoque etiam  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>para . . . , kata,</FOREIGN>  etc.
respondet:  <HI REND="ITALIC">þairharbaidjan, þairhbairan, þairhgaggan,
