subordinatis sententiis;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæra</FOREIGN> : Cor. I, XV, 14  <HI REND="ITALIC">jabai
xristus ni urrais, svare þau jas-so mereins unsara;</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæn</FOREIGN> :
Luc. IX, 46;  <HI REND="ITALIC">galaiþ mitons ïn ïns þata, warjis þau ïze
maists vesi;</HI>  Cor. I, VII, 5  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mhú ajpostereiðte</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ïzvara misso,
niba þau us gaqissai;</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv</FOREIGN> : Cor. I, XV, 29, 30  <HI REND="ITALIC">jabai
allis dauþans ni urreisand, duwe þau daupjand faur
ïns. duwe þau veis bireikjai sijum;</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaæn</FOREIGN> : Cor. II,
XI, 16  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïbai was mik muni unfropana. aiþþau vaila
þau sve unfrodana nimaiþ;</HI>  Mc. VI, 56  <HI REND="ITALIC">bedun ïna ei
þau skauta vastjos ïs attaitokeina.</HI>  Sic etiam ubi Graecus
nullam particulam respondentem usurpavit:
Phlpp. III, 13  <HI REND="ITALIC">broþrjus ïk mik silban ni þau man
gatahan;</HI>  I, 22  <HI REND="ITALIC">wa þau valjau, ni kann;</HI>  Luc. XVI,
4  <HI REND="ITALIC">andþahta mik wa taujau, ei þau, biþe afsatjaidau
is fauragaggja, andnimaina mik;</HI>  2) in consequente
hypotheticarum sententiarum, ubi respondet
graeco  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæn</FOREIGN> : Mc. XIII, 20  <HI REND="ITALIC">ni frauja gamaurgidedi
