ur,</HI>  suec.  <HI REND="ITALIC">öfver,</HI>  angl., dan., batav.  <HI REND="ITALIC">over,</HI>  rec. sup.
germ.  <HI REND="ITALIC">über;</HI>  gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpevr,</FOREIGN>  lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">super;</HI>  coll.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Uf;</HI>  Bopp 80,
83; Gr. IV, 789; Gf. I, 78;  <HI REND="ITALIC">Alth. Praepos.</HI>  156; Rchth.
1108), praepositio cum accusativo et dativo constructa,
quae respectum superioritatis designat eodemque
modo ad  <HI REND="ITALIC">uf</HI>  refertur atque graecum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpevr</FOREIGN>  ad
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpov.</FOREIGN></ITEM> <ITEM>I.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Praepositio:</HI>  A. cum accusativo: 1) localis, super,
a) super aliquid (stare super): Luc. IV, 39
 <HI REND="ITALIC">atstandans ufar</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpavnw</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïja;</HI>  Eph. IV, 10  <HI REND="ITALIC">ussteigan
ufar</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpavnw</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">allans himinans;</HI>  b) super, trans,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pevran</FOREIGN> :
Joan. VI, 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïesus galaiþ ufar marein;</HI>  17; X, 40; XVIII,
1; 2) metaphorice, a) super, Eph. I, 22  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïna atgaf
haubiþ ufar</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpevr</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">alla aikklesjon;</HI>  Thess. II, II, 4
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ufarhafjands sik ufar</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiv</FOREIGN>  c. accus.)  <HI REND="ITALIC">all;</HI>  b) super, insuper,
progrediens et praecedentibus adjiciens,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiv</FOREIGN> 
c. dat.: Eph. VI, 16  <HI REND="ITALIC">ufar all andnimands skildu galaubeinais;</HI> 
Col. III, 14  <HI REND="ITALIC">ufar alla gahamoþ ïzvis friaþva;</HI> 
c) super, prae, cum significatione comparativa,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpevr</FOREIGN> 
c. accus.: Mth. X, 37  <HI REND="ITALIC">saei frijoþ attan aiþþau aiþein
ufar mik;</HI>  Luc. VI, 40; Cor. II, XII, 13; Philem. 16;
Neh. VII, 2; Skeir. VII, b; Cor. II, I, 8  <HI REND="ITALIC">ufar maht;</HI> 
VIII, 3; Skeir. VI, b  <HI REND="ITALIC">attins veitvodei all ufar ïnsaht
manniskodaus ïohannes unandsok undredan mag kunþi;
ufar all</HI>  Eph. III, 20;  <HI REND="ITALIC">ufar þatei</HI>  Luc. III, 13; Cor.
 <COL N="1424"></COL> I, IV, 6; Cor. II, XII, 6;  <HI REND="ITALIC">ufar mikil</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">ufar filu,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJperlivan</FOREIGN> :
Cor. II, XI, 5; XII, 11.</ITEM> <ITEM>B. Cum dativo: 1) localis, super, a) super aliquid,
sursum, in sola formula  <HI REND="ITALIC">atta ïzvar sa ufar himinam</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ oujravnioû</FOREIGN> ) Mth. VI, 14, 26, 32, coll.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In;</HI>  b) super,
in (se extendere),  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiv</FOREIGN>  c. accus.: Mth. XXVII, 45  <HI REND="ITALIC">varþ
riqis ufar allai airþai;</HI>  2) metaphorice, super, in,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpevr</FOREIGN>  c. accus.: Mth. X, 24  <HI REND="ITALIC">nist siponeis ufar laisarja;</HI> 
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiv</FOREIGN>  c. genit.: Rom. IX, 5  <HI REND="ITALIC">saei ïst ufar allaim guþ;</HI>  Eph.
IV, 6;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiv</FOREIGN>  c. accus. post  <HI REND="ITALIC">þiudanon</HI>  Luc. I, 33; XIX,
14, 27;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpavnw</FOREIGN>  post  <HI REND="ITALIC">valdufni haban</HI>  Luc. XIX, 17 et
 <HI REND="ITALIC">valdufni giban</HI>  Luc. IX, 1.</ITEM> <ITEM>II. In compositione: 1) cum verbis:  <HI REND="ITALIC">ufargaggan,
