Cor. I, XIII, 12,  <HI REND="ITALIC">andvairþi viþra andvairþi;</HI>  Mc. IV, 1
 <HI REND="ITALIC">managei viþra marein ana staþa vas; </HI> 15 <HI REND="ITALIC"> þai viþra
vig;</HI>  Luc. VIII, 12; I, 73  <HI REND="ITALIC">guþ aiþ svor viþra abrahama;</HI> 
Cor, II, V, 12  <HI REND="ITALIC">viþra ainana wopan;</HI>  VII, 12  <HI REND="ITALIC">gabairhtjan
usdaudein viþra ïzvis</HI>  (ubi in interpretatione
nostra loco  <HI REND="ITALIC">erga vos</HI>  legendum est  <HI REND="ITALIC">coram vobis</HI> ); XII,
19  <HI REND="ITALIC">sunjon sik viþra ïzvis</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJmiðn</FOREIGN> ); sic Mth. VIII, 34
 <HI REND="ITALIC">usïddja viþra ïesu,</HI>  vertitur: ivit obviam Jesu ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxhðlqen
eijû sunavnthsin twðé 1Ihsouð</FOREIGN> ); 2) in metaphorico sensu
usurpatur: a) in bonam partem, pro, ob,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>provû</FOREIGN>  (c.
acc.): Thess. 1, V, 14  <HI REND="ITALIC">usbeisneigs visan viþra allans;</HI> 
Tim. II, II, 24  <HI REND="ITALIC">qairrus visan viþra allans;</HI>  Gal. VI, 10
 <HI REND="ITALIC">vaurkjan þiuþ viþra allans;</HI>  Eph. VI, 9  <HI REND="ITALIC">þiuþ taujaiþ
viþra ïns;</HI>  Thess. I, V, 5  <HI REND="ITALIC">þiuþ laistjaiþ viþra allans;</HI> 
b) in malam partem, contra, adversus,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>provû</FOREIGN>  (c. acc.):
Col. III, 19  <HI REND="ITALIC">baitrs visan viþra ainana;</HI>  Cor. I, VI, 1  <HI REND="ITALIC">viþra
anþarana staua haban;</HI>  Col. III, 13  <HI REND="ITALIC">haban fairina;</HI> 
Eph. VI, 11  <HI REND="ITALIC">standan;</HI>  Luc. XIV, 31  <HI REND="ITALIC">stigqan viþra anþarana</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sumbavllein eJtevrwé</FOREIGN> ); Eph. VI, 12  <HI REND="ITALIC">brakja viþra</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>provû</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">bloþ;</HI>  Mc. X, 5  <HI REND="ITALIC">viþra harduhairtein gameljan
anabusn;</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katav</FOREIGN>  (c. genit.):  <HI REND="ITALIC">viþra ïzvis ïst;</HI>  Luc. IX, 50;
Cor. II, X, 5  <HI REND="ITALIC">ushafjan sik;</HI>  XIII, 8  <HI REND="ITALIC">magan wa;</HI>  Mc. XI,
25  <HI REND="ITALIC">wa haban;</HI>  Mth. X, 35  <HI REND="ITALIC">skaidan mannan viþra attan;</HI> 
Gal. V, 17  <HI REND="ITALIC">leik gairneiþ viþra ahman;</HI>  XXIII  <HI REND="ITALIC">viþra þo
svaleika nist vitoþ;</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiv</FOREIGN>  (c. accus.): Mc. III, 24, 25
 <HI REND="ITALIC">þiudangardi viþra sik gadailjada;</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû</FOREIGN> : Cor. I, VIII, 12
 <HI REND="ITALIC">fravaurkjan viþra broþruns;</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parav</FOREIGN>  (c. accus.): Skeir.
I, c  <HI REND="ITALIC">þata ïst viþra þata gadob;</HI>  hinc etiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">andhafjan
viþra,</HI>  denegare, obstare, ita ut alterius sermo impugnetur,
vel saltem ut falsus declaretur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>provû</FOREIGN>  (c.
acc.): Luc. IV, 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">andhof ïesus viþra ïns;</HI>  VI, 3; Skeir.
VIII, b; Mth. XXVII, 14  <HI REND="ITALIC">andhof vïþra ni ainhun vaurde;</HI> 
