130 sqq., Rchth. 728, 751), praepositiones, quarum
prior respectum localem, coram, ante, temporalem,
ante, et moralem, pro, posterior vero localem
tantum et moralem designat.</ITEM> <ITEM>1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Faur:</HI>  A. Praepositio accusativum regens, significat
a) localiter, ad, prae (ita ut objectum aliud
antecedat),  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parav</FOREIGN> : c. accus.: Mc. I, 16  <HI REND="ITALIC">warbonds faur
marein;</HI>  item post  <HI REND="ITALIC">galeiþan</HI>  Mc. II, 13;  <HI REND="ITALIC">gadriusan</HI>  IV,
4; Luc. VIII, 5;  <HI REND="ITALIC">sitan</HI>  Mc. X, 46; Luc. XVIII, 35;
hinc  <HI REND="ITALIC">sa faur marein</HI>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paravlioû</FOREIGN> : Luc. VI, 17; etiam
Mc. VIII, 6  <HI REND="ITALIC">atlagidedun faur þo managein,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parevqhkan
twðé oæclwé</FOREIGN> ; semel adest Mc. XIV, 68  <HI REND="ITALIC">galaiþ faur gard,</HI> 
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxhðlqen eiúû toú proauvlion</FOREIGN> ; b) temporaliter,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prov</FOREIGN> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">faur
mel</HI>  Mth. VIII, 29; Cor. I, IV, 5; Skier. VIII, a;  <HI REND="ITALIC">faur
mela aiveina</HI>  Tim. II, I, 9; Tit. I, 2;  <HI REND="ITALIC">faur jera fidvortaihun</HI> 
Cor. II, XII, 2;  <HI REND="ITALIC">faur gaskaft fairwaus</HI>  Joan.
XVII, 24;  <HI REND="ITALIC">faur gasatein fairwaus</HI>  Eph. I, 4;  <HI REND="ITALIC">faur hanins
hruk</HI>  Mth. XXVI, 75;  <HI REND="ITALIC">faur þata</HI>  Skeir. III, a; hinc
Thess. I, IV, 15  <HI REND="ITALIC">ni bisnivam faur þans anaslepandans</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouj mhú pqavswmen touúû koimhqevntaû</FOREIGN> :); c) metaphorice
post verba omnis generis et locutiones, quae factum,
passionem, orationem, etc., pro aliquo fieri indicant,
sive ad designandum finem, vel rationem, vel substitutionem,
pro,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpevr</FOREIGN>  c. genit.: Mc. IX, 40 ( <HI REND="ITALIC">saei nist
viþra ïzvis, faur ïzvis ïst</HI> ); X, 45 ( <HI REND="ITALIC">giban saivala faur managans
saun</HI> ); Luc. IX, 50; Joan. X, 11, 15; XIII, 37,
38; XV, 13; XVIII, 14; Rom. VIII, 15; IX, 3; XIV, 15;
Cor. I, IV, 6; V, 7; XV, 3, 29; Cor. II, I, 6, 11; V, 15,
20, 21; VII, 7, 8, 12; VIII, 16, 24; IX, 14; XII, 5, 10,
15; XIII, 8; Gal. I, 4; II, 20; Eph. III, 10; V, 2, 25;
VI, 20; Phlpp. I, 29; IV, 10; Col. I, 7, 9, 24; Thess.
I, V, 10; Tim. I, II, 6; Philem. 13; Skeir. I, a; II, a;
VIII, c, d.</ITEM> <ITEM>B. Adverbium: Mc. VIII, 6  <HI REND="ITALIC">atlagjan faur</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paratiqevnai</FOREIGN> );
Luc. XIX, 4  <HI REND="ITALIC">biþragjan faur</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>protrevcein</FOREIGN> ).</ITEM> <ITEM>C. In compositione: a) cum verbis:  <HI REND="ITALIC">faurbiudan,
faurgaggan, faurdammjan, faurqiþan, faurlagjan,
faurmuljan, faurrinnan, faursigljan, faursnivan, faurvalvjan,
faurvaipjan;</HI>  bicomposita:  <HI REND="ITALIC">faurbigaggan,
faurbiþragjan, faurbisnivan;</HI>  b) cum substantivis:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">faurbauhts, faurhah, faurlageins, faurstasseis;</HI>  c)
cum adjectivo:  <HI REND="ITALIC">unfaurveis.</HI></ITEM> <ITEM>II.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Faura:</HI>  A. Praepositio dativum regens, significat
a) localiter, coram,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæmprosqen</FOREIGN> : Mth. VI, 2 ( <HI REND="ITALIC">ni haurnjais
faura þus</HI> ); XI, 10 ( <HI REND="ITALIC">aggilus gamanveiþ vig þeinana
faura þus</HI> ); XXVI, 70; XXVII, 11; Mc. I, 2; Luc. V,
29; XIX, 27; Joan. X, 4; Cor. II, V, 10; Gal. II, 14;
Thess. I, III, 9, 13; Neh. V, 15;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejnwvpion</FOREIGN> : Luc. XIV,
10;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katenwvpion</FOREIGN> : Col. I, 22;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>proú proûwvpou</FOREIGN> : Mth. XI,
10; Mc. I, 2; Luc. IX, 52; quae formula etiam per
 <HI REND="ITALIC">faura andvairþja</HI>  exprimitur Luc. I, 76; VII, 27; X, 1;
Neh. V, 15; quod etiam pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejnantivon</FOREIGN> : Mc. II, 12 ponitur;
insuper adhibetur  <HI REND="ITALIC">faura,</HI>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katav</FOREIGN>  c. accus.:
Gal. III, 1;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parav</FOREIGN>  c. accus.: Mc. V, 21; Luc. VII, 38;
VIII, 4, 37; XVII, 16;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parav</FOREIGN>  c. dat.: Luc. IX, 47; hinc
Luc. II, 22  <HI REND="ITALIC">atsatjan faura fraujin</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paristavnai twðé kurivwé</FOREIGN> );
Rom. XIV, 10  <HI REND="ITALIC">gasatjan faura stauastola</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paristavnai twðé
bhvmati</FOREIGN> ); coll. Cor. I, XV, 28  <HI REND="ITALIC">gakunnan sik faura ainamma</HI> 
( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpotavssesqai tini</FOREIGN> ); Tim. I, II, 12  <HI REND="ITALIC">fraujinon
faura vaira</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujqenteiðn ajndrovû</FOREIGN> ), quod loco: coram, in
conspectu hominis (vid. ad h. l.) etiam verti potest:
super, magis quam homo, ut saltem Col. I, 17  <HI REND="ITALIC">ïs ïst
faura</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prov</FOREIGN> )  <HI REND="ITALIC">allaim</HI>  explicandus est; b) metaphorice, ante,
prae, post verba administrandi, fugiendi, abscondendi,
praeservandi, et similium,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpov</FOREIGN> : Mth. VII, 15 ( <HI REND="ITALIC">atsaiwiþ
 <COL N="1496"></COL> faura liugnapraufetum</HI> ); Mc. XII, 38; XIV, 52;
Luc. III, 7; IX, 45; X, 21; XIX, 42; XX, 46; Joan. X, 5;
XII, 36;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejk</FOREIGN> : Joan. XVII, 15; ob, propter, prae,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpov</FOREIGN> :
Luc. XIX, 5  <HI REND="ITALIC">ni mahta ïesu gasaiwan faura managein;</HI> 
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>diaú</FOREIGN>  c. accus.: Joan. XII, 42  <HI REND="ITALIC">faura fareisaium ni andhaihaitun;</HI> 
prae, praestantiam indicans, vid. supra a)
fin.</ITEM> <ITEM>B. Adverbium: 1) ante,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæmprosqen</FOREIGN> : Phlpp. III, 14;
2) prius,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>provteron</FOREIGN> : Tim. I, I, 13; Skeir. I, c; 3) pro
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prov </FOREIGN>  in compositione, ut:  <HI REND="ITALIC">faura dustodjan,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>proenavrcesqai</FOREIGN> :
